\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10512\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2025 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2025 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 11/16: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOGE, MATIC, DOT, UNI, LTC\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,836 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 November 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Traders are selling at the top of each bounce and rally, suggesting that crypto \b \highlight22\uc2 investor sentiment\b0 \highlight\uc2  is tilted toward more downside.\par \par \uc2 The collapse of the FTX cryptocurrency exchange has created a liquidity crisis in the crypto space, which could extend the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ftx-crisis-could-extend-crypto-winter-to-the-end-of-2023-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crypto winter through the end of 2023  }}}\uc2 , according to a research report by \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 According to analysts, the FTX implosion could keep institutional investors at bay because they are even more likely to tread cautiously for some time.\par \par \uc2 The crisis has negatively impacted several crypto-focused companies that have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ftx-bankruptcy-freezes-millions-worth-of-crypto-company-funds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assets stuck on FTX  }}}\uc2  following the company\u8217\'20\'19s bankruptcy filing on Nov. 11. Investors also fear the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/breaking-crypto-lender-genesis-global-halts-withdrawals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contagion could spread  }}}\uc2 , causing further damage to the cryptocurrency ecosystem.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-11/7445dc66-d769-4d7d-ba19-6417b34aeed6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.  }}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Although several investors were rattled by the collapse of FTX, billionaire venture capitalist and serial blockchain investor Tim Draper remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Bitcoin ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC  }}}\uc2  ). In a Nov.15 interview with Cointelegraph, Draper doubled down on his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/tim-draper-still-positive-on-250k-bitcoin-price-prediction-in-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $250,000 target for Bitcoin in 2023  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, investors should take the price projection with a pinch of salt because it is unlikely that Bitcoin will start a roaring {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/trading-for-beginners/bull-vs-bear-crypto-market-what-is-the-difference-and-how-to-handle-both"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bull market  }}}\uc2  in the near future.\par \par \uc2 What are the key support and resistance levels to watch out for on Bitcoin and altcoins? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin broke and closed below the June low of $17,622 on Nov. 9. This marked the resumption of the downtrend. Although the bulls tried to stage a strong recovery on Nov. 10, their efforts met with heavy selling above $17,622. This suggests that the bears have flipped the level into resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-11/fe2bd8e9-fb23-4e1a-acb3-7727f7fb2d38.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.  }}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) of $18,271 has turned down and the relative strength index (RSI) is in the negative territory. This suggests that the bears have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains below $17,622, it will increase the prospect of a break below $15,588, If that happens, the BTC/Tether ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/tether"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDT  }}}\uc2  ) pair could extend its decline to $12,200.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns up and breaks above the 20-day EMA, it will suggest strong demand at lower levels. The pair could then challenge the psychological level at $20,000.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH  }}}\uc2  ) has been declining inside a descending channel pattern for the past several weeks. The failure to push the price above the channel on Nov. 4 may have led to profit-booking by the short-term traders.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-11/ddddc02b-0c01-40e5-a2ec-02fc530f3217.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.  }}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The buyers aggressively bought the dip to the support line on Nov. 10, but the relief rally fizzled out near the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) of $1,372. This suggests that the bears are selling at higher levels.\par \par \uc2 The bears will again strive to sink the price below the channel. If that happens, the selling could intensify and the ETH/USDT pair could drop to $1,000. To gain the upper hand, buyers will have to push the price above the moving averages. The pair could then rise to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 BNB ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB  }}}\uc2  ) soared to $398 on Nov. 8, but the bulls could not sustain the higher levels as seen from the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick. The selling continued on Nov. 9 and pulled the price near the strong support at $258.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-11/2ff5a89f-7b19-4d49-8804-c55721071046.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.  }}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls purchased the drop on Nov. 10, but they could not thrust the price above the 20-day EMA of $295. This suggests that the sentiment turned negative and the bears were selling the relief rallies to the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 The bears will again try to break the support at $258 and if they manage to do that, the BNB/USDT pair could drop to $239 and later to $216. This negative view will be invalidated in the near term if thebulls push and sustain the price above $313.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 XRP ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP  }}}\uc2  ) re-entered the $0.41 to $0.30 range on Nov. 8, indicating a lack of demand at higher levels. The selling continued on Nov. 9 and the price dropped to $0.32.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-11/02359284-fa5d-4b5b-a731-f4da81e5d029.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.  }}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Buyers purchased the dip and tried to push the price back above $0.41 but the bears did not relent. This suggests that the bears have flipped the $0.41 level into resistance. The bears will again try to pull the pair to the critical support at $0.30.\par \par \uc2 This is an important level for the bulls to defend because a break and close below it could signal the resumption of the downtrend. On the upside, the first sign of strength will be a break and close above $0.41. The XRP/USDT pair could then rise to the 50-day SMA of $0.45.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) is in a strong downtrend. Although both moving averages are sloping down, the RSI is attempting to form a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  divergence, indicating that the selling pressure may be reducing.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-11/6cbeabd7-9b14-403c-b12b-df600679a8fa.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.  }}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The first sign of strength will be a break and close above the downtrend line. Such a move will suggest a potential trend change. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could then attempt a rally to $0.52.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price continues lower and breaks below $0.31, the pair could drop to the support line. This line has arrested the decline on three previous occasions, hence the bulls may again buy the dip to this level. If buyers fail to defend the level, the pair could extend its downtrend to $0.25.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE  }}}\uc2  ) witnessed a sharp rally from $0.06 on Oct. 25 to $0.16 on Nov. 1. That pushed the RSI into extremely overbought levels, which may have tempted short-term traders to book profits.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-11/db9b6ed2-87e0-4394-b484-6b4e4e181bc9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.  }}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The selling picked up momentum after the bulls failed to defend the 50% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.11. Buyers defended the 50-day SMA of $0.08 on Nov. 9, but the bears halted the recovery at the 20-day EMA of $0.09.\par \par \uc2 The DOGE/USDT pair has been trading between the moving averages for the past few days. If the bears sink the price below the 50-day SMA, the pair could complete a 100% retracement and drop to $0.06. Contrarily, a break above $0.10 will suggest that the bulls are back in the game. The pair could then rise to $0.12.\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polygon ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC  }}}\uc2  ) soared above the overhead resistance of $1.05 on Nov. 4, but the rally met with stiff resistance at $1.30 on Nov. 5. Buyers tried to resume the up-move on Nov. 7 but could not clear the overhead hurdle.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-11/19d1701a-96e5-4f14-a2a7-ee36a1e2615d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.  }}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears sold aggressively on Nov. 8 and 9 and pulled the price below the moving averages, but the buyers held the uptrend line. The MATIC/USDT pair rebounded sharply on Nov. 10, but the bears sold at higher levels and pulled the price back below the 20-day EMA of $0.96 on Nov. 12.\par \par \uc2 If the price slides below the 50-day SMA of $0.89, the pair could drop to the uptrend line. A break below this support could open the doors for a retest of the crucial support at $0.69. On the contrary, if buyers push the price above the 20-day EMA, the pair could rise to $1.05.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-dips-to-16-4k-over-genesis-woes-as-execs-defend-gbtc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin price dips to $16.4K over Genesis woes as execs defend GBTC  }}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT  }}}\uc2  ) plunged below the strong support zone of $6 to $5.68 on Nov. 9. This indicates the resumption of the downtrend.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-11/55489e45-5c85-45a2-a926-e99d594cb85a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.  }}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Buyers attempted to push the price back above $6 and trap the aggressive bears but the sellers held their ground. This indicates that the bears are trying to flip the $6 level into resistance.\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA of $6.12 and the RSI in the negative territory indicate an advantage to the bears. The sellers will make one more attempt to pull the DOT/USDT pair below $5.32. If they succeed, the pair could extend its decline to $4.32. To invalidate this negative view, the bulls will have to push and sustain the price above the moving averages.\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT\par \par \uc2 Uniswap ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/uniswap-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UNI  }}}\uc2  ) had been trading between $5.14 and $7.36 for the past several days. Buyers drove the price above the resistance on Nov. 4 but could not build upon this advantage. The bears pulled the price back into the range on Nov. 6.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-11/f805ed3a-a8d7-435a-b31f-62bf5645ee59.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.  }}}\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This may have trapped the aggressive bulls who then rushed to the exit. Long liquidation and selling by the bears pulled the price below the support of $5.14 on Nov. 8 but this proved to be a bear trap. The bulls bought the dip and pushed the price back into the range on Nov. 10.\par \par \uc2 The recovery is facing stiff resistance at the moving averages, indicating selling at higher levels. The bears may again attempt to sink and sustain the price below the range but the bulls are expected to defend the support aggressively.\par \par \uc2 This suggests that the UNI/USDT pair may remain range-bound between $4.71 and $7.79 for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC  }}}\uc2  ) has been range-bound between $46 and $75 for the past several weeks. The failure of the bulls to push the price above $75 on Nov. 7 may have attracted profit-booking by short-term traders. That pulled the price near the support of $46 on Nov. 9.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-11/2957a216-41a8-4199-bd3a-e824d40f43d6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.  }}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 When the price is stuck inside a range, traders generally buy the dips to the support level and that is what happened on Nov. 10. The LTC/USDT pair continued its rise on Nov. 11 but met with strong selling near $65. This suggests that the bears are active at higher levels.\par \par \uc2 The flattish moving averages and the RSI near the midpoint indicate a balance between supply and demand. This indicates that the pair could trade in a tight range between $53 and $65 for some time.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph.com. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMTEvOTU3ZTA2YTctMDFkNy00MmJhLThlZTgtNTQ2YmQ5MDU4NmMyLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020221117eibg0000a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
