o keep an eye on while Bitcoin price consolidates\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Big Smokey \par \uc2 978 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 October 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price is stuck in a downtrend, but other assets are beginning to show shoots of green.\par \par \uc2 This week, Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) price took a tumble as a hotter-than-expected consumer price index (CPI) report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-is-the-crypto-market-down-today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 showed high inflation remains a persistent challenge}}}\uc2  despite a wave of interest rate hikes from the \uc2 United States Federal Reserve\uc2 . Interestingly, the market\u8217\'20\'19s negative reaction to a high CPI print seemed priced in by investors, and BTC\u8217\'20\'19s and Ether\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) prices reclaimed all of their intraday losses to close the day in the black.\par \par \uc2 A quick look at Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s market structure shows that even with the post-CPI print drop, the price continues to trade in the same price range it has been in for the past 122 days. Adding to this dynamic, Cointelegraph market analyst Ray Salmond {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-analysts-and-traders-say-btc-s-low-volatility-is-a-calm-before-the-storm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported on a unique situation}}}\uc2  where Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s futures open interest is at a record high, while its \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also near record lows.\par \par \uc2 These factors, along with other indicators, have historically preceded explosive price movements, but history will also show that predicting the direction of these moves is nearly impossible.\par \par \uc2 So, aside from multiple metrics hinting that a decisive price move is brewing, Bitcoin is still doing more of the same thing it\u8217\'20\'19s done for the past 4.5 months. With that being the case, it is perhaps time to start looking elsewhere for emerging trends and possible opportunities.\par \par \uc2 Here are a few data points that I\u8217\'20\'19ve continued to be intrigued by.\par \par \uc2 New rotations will emerge\par \par \uc2 ETH\u8217\'20\'19s price has lost its luster in the now post-Merge era, and the asset now reflects the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend that dominates the rest of the market. Since the Merge, ETH\u8217\'20\'19s price is down 30% from its $2,000 high, and it\u8217\'20\'19s likely that a good deal of the speculative capital that backed the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  Merge narrative is now in stablecoins looking for the next investment opportunity.\par \par \uc2 Aside from ETH being an asymmetrical performer in the last four months, Cosmos ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/cosmos-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM}}}\uc2  ) also defied the market downtrend by posting a monster rally from $5.40 to $16.85. As covered thoroughly by Cointelegraph, oversold conditions, along with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/most-of-the-crypto-market-is-down-but-cosmos-atom-price-is-up-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hype of Cosmos 2.0}}}\uc2 , backed the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  price action seen in the altcoin, but this chart continues to capture my imagination.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/c143a3ab-fc00-474d-a969-ab5033906696.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ATOM emissions schedule (old vs. new). Source: Cosmos Hub\par \par \uc2 According to the revised Cosmos white paper, the current supply of ATOM will dynamically adjust based on the supply and demand of its staking. As shown in the chart above, when Cosmos 2.0 \u8220\'20\'1Ckicks in\u8221\'20\'1D for the first 10 months, issuance of new ATOM tokens is high, but after the 36th month, the asset becomes deflationary.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/f19b2cab-8fcd-46de-a527-71d5b87e4906.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ATOM/USDT 3-day chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 From the vantage point of technical analysis, ATOM\u8217\'20\'19s price appears to have hit a local top as the months leading up to Cosmos 2.0 were a \u8220\'20\'1Cbuy the rumor, sell the news\u8221\'20\'1D type of event, but it will be interesting to see what transpires with ATOM\u8217\'20\'19s price as the market approaches month 20 in the diagram above.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/price-analysis-10-14-spx-dxy-btc-eth-bnb-xrp-ada-sol-doge-matic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 10/14: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , SOL, DOGE, MATIC}}}\par \par \uc2 Keep an eye on Ethereum Network activity\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/e403f2cb-dc19-488a-ac26-e750f12353af.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Ether emissions plummet post Merge. Source: Delphi Digital\par \par \uc2 Since the Ethereum Merge, Ether emissions have dropped by 97%, and while the price has pulled back significantly, over the coming months, investors might keep an eye on Ethereum network activity, developments with ETH staking across decentralized finance (DeFi) and institutional products, along with any spikes in gas (connected to network activity).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/30cd749d-3394-42e2-9fd2-32341a606675.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Ether supply dynamics. Source: Delphi Digital\par \par \uc2 While the price could succumb to \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  pressure in the short term, if the market begins to turn around if new trends trigger increased use of DeFi products, it\u8217\'20\'19s possible that ETH\u8217\'20\'19s price {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/what-s-next-for-bitcoin-and-the-crypto-market-now-that-the-ethereum-merge-is-over"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could react positively}}}\uc2  to those developments.\par \par \uc2 Post-Merge, BTC price action will likely remain king\par \par \uc2 While {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bigsmokey.substack.com/p/smoke-signals-where-are-they-coming"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new trends}}}\uc2  across various altcoins may emerge, it\u8217\'20\'19s important to remember the wider context in which crypto assets exist. Global economies are on the rocks, and persistently high inflation remains an issue in the United States and many other countries. Bond prices are whipsawing, and a looming debt crisis makes its presence known on a daily basis. Risk-on assets like cryptocurrencies are incredibly volatile, and even the strongest price trends in crypto (whether backed by fundamentals or not) are subject to the whimsy of macro factors such as equities markets, geopolitics and other market events that impact investors\u8217\'20\'19 sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Keeping this in mind, Bitcoin remains the largest asset by market capitalization within the crypto sector, and any sharp moves from BTC\u8217\'20\'19s price are bound to support or suppress the micro trends that might be gaining traction in the market. There is still the possibility of a sharp downside in Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s price, so traders are encouraged to calculate investment size according to their own appetite for risk, and while multiple metrics might support opening long positions in various crypto assets, it still seems too early to fully ape in.\par \par \uc2 This newsletter was written by Big Smokey, the author of The Humble Pontificator Substack and resident newsletter author at Cointelegraph. Each Friday, Big Smokey will write market insights, trending how-tos, analyses and early-bird research on potential emerging trends within the crypto market.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph.com. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMTAvMzVhNWY5MzktMDQ4ZS00MjYwLTgwOTItNzcxNWJhYWRlMTZkLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020221014eiae000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/14: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, DOGE, MATIC\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,824 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 October 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The bulls' failure to sustain higher levels on Oct. 14 means the bottom is unconfirmed in the U.S. equities markets and cryptocurrencies.\par \par \uc2 The United States Consumer Price Index (CPI) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-hits-3-week-lows-on-us-cpi-as-bitcoin-liquidates-57m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased 8.2% annually}}}\uc2  in September, beating economists\u8217\'20\'19 expectations of an 8.1% rise. The CPI print lived up to its hype and caused a sharp, but short-term increase in volatile risk assets.\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 oscillated inside its widest trading range since 2020 and Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) also witnessed a large intraday range of more than $1,323 on Oct. 13. However, Bitcoin still could not shake out of the $18,125 to $20,500 range in which it has been for the past several days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/6c0e9e1a-a5c4-4fb4-8dd5-e0a68e72ee4d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Both the U.S. equities markets and Bitcoin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-bear-trap-sees-btc-price-near-20k-as-daily-gains-top-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tried to extend their recovery}}}\uc2  on Oct. 14 but the higher levels attracted selling, indicating that the bears have not yet given up.\par \par \uc2 Could the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-markets-to-see-explosive-volatility-soon-arcane-research"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased \b  \highlight22volatility\b0 \highlight22  culminate with a breakout}}}\uc2  to the upside or will it start the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-traders-were-ready-for-a-hot-cpi-report-but-btc-bears-are-still-in-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 next leg of the downtrend}}}\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the S&P 500 index, the U.S. dollar index (DXY) and the major cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 SPX\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 index (SPX) gapped down on Oct. 13 and dropped to $3,491 but lower levels attracted huge buying by the bulls. That may have caught several aggressive bears on the wrong paw and they might have scrambled to cover their short positions. That propelled the index back above the breakdown level of $3,636.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/2d1af713-df9c-4aec-a4ec-ff7381c2bcb8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SPX daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Buyers tried to extend the recovery on Oct. 14, but the bears had other plans. The sellers vigorously defended the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($3,715), indicating that the sentiment remains negative and relief rallies are being sold into.\par \par \uc2 The bears will try to sink the index to $3,491, which is an important level to keep an eye on. If this support cracks, the index could dive to $3,325.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the index rebounds off the support zone between $3,636 and $3,491, it will suggest that bulls may be accumulating on dips. Buyers will then attempt to overcome the barrier at the 20-day EMA and challenge the downtrend line. If this resistance collapses, it will signal that the corrective phase may be over.\par \par \uc2 DXY\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar index turned down from $113.92 on Oct. 13 but the bulls arrested the decline at the 20-day EMA (112). This suggests that the sentiment remains positive and traders are viewing the dips as a buying opportunity.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/372bb6db-42d1-40d6-b452-3a5aebdb164f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DXY daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will try to pierce the overhead resistance zone between $113.92 and $114.77. An acceptance above this zone will signal the resumption of the uptrend. The index could then rally to $117.14.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the overhead resistance, the bears will try to pull the index below the 20-day EMA. A break below this support will be the first indication that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum is weakening.\par \par \uc2 The index could then decline to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) (109). A trend change will be signaled if bears sink the price below the uptrend line.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin sliced through the support at $18,843 on Oct. 13 and dipped close to $18,125. This level attracted buying, which started a sharp recovery as seen from the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/f61ecfb0-bc89-4d28-bc66-7301213bd3e5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Buyers pushed the price above the moving averages on Oct. 14 but the up-move is facing stiff resistance at the downtrend line. The 20-day EMA ($19,466) is flattening out and the relative strength index (RSI) is near the midpoint, indicating equilibrium between buyers and sellers.\par \par \uc2 This balance will tilt in favor of the bulls if they push and sustain the price above the overhead resistance at $20,500. The BTC/USDT pair could then rally to $22,800. The bears are expected to mount a stiff resistance at this level.\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains below the 20-day EMA, the bears will again try to pull the pair below $18,843 and challenge the support at $18,125.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) broke below the support at $1,220 on Oct. 13 but the bears could not keep the price down. The bulls vigorously purchased the dip, forming a hammer candlestick pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/01ee1a58-fc76-4daf-aca3-ba79d7b699a1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Buyers have sustained the positive momentum on Oct. 14 and are trying to push the price above the overhead zone between the 20-day EMA ($1,331) and the resistance line of the triangle.\par \par \uc2 If they can pull it off, the ETH/USDT pair could attempt a rally to the downtrend line of the descending channel pattern. The bulls will have to clear this obstacle to signal a potential trend change.\par \par \uc2 The bears are likely to have other plans. They will attempt to halt the recovery in the overhead zone and then try to pull the pair below $1,190.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  has been range-bound between $300 and $258 for the past several days. In a range, traders usually buy near the support and sell close to the resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/08ce9ddf-d96b-45cd-a88c-13210c11af36.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 That is what happened on Oct. 13 as the bulls purchased the dip to $258. Buyers tried to push the price above the moving averages on Oct. 14 but the long wick on the candlestick shows that bears are selling near resistance levels. The bears will again try to pull the price below $258 and extend the decline to $216.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns up and breaks above the moving averages, the BNB/USDT pair could attempt a rally to the overhead resistance at $300. A break above this level could set the stage for a rally to $338.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) broke below the 20-day EMA ($0.47) on Oct. 13 but the bears could not sustain the lower levels. The bulls purchased the dip and pushed the price back above the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/3f8cf224-895b-4a1f-9079-3c218abf995e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping up and the RSI is in the positive territory, indicating advantage to buyers. The bulls will attempt to push the price above the overhead resistance at $0.56. If that happens, the XRP/USDT pair could resume its uptrend and rally toward the next overhead resistance at $0.66.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of weakness will be a break and close below the 20-day EMA. That would indicate that traders may be booking profits at higher levels. The pair could then slide to the breakout level of $0.41.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) found buying support at $0.35 on Oct. 13 but the bulls are struggling to push the price above the breakdown level of $0.40 on Oct. 14.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/1d1864e5-e089-4550-92d1-6e3cd7a46153.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.41) continues to slope down and the RSI is in the oversold territory, indicating that bears are in control. If the price continues lower and breaks below $0.35, it will suggest that bears have flipped $0.40 into resistance. That could increase the likelihood of a drop to $0.33.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view could be negated in the near term if buyers push the price above the moving averages. That will indicate strong accumulation at lower levels. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could then climb to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-bear-market-will-last-2-3-months-max-interview-with-btc-analyst-philip-swift"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin bear market will last '2-3 months max' \u8212\'20\'14Interview with BTC analyst Philip Swift}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) plunged below the $30 support on Oct. 13 but the bears could not build upon this strength and sink the price to the vital support at $26. The bulls arrested the drop at $27.87 and pushed the price back above $30.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/270bd4da-098b-4601-aa3d-a5907e626b9a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Buyers tried to extend the positive momentum on Oct. 14 but ran into heavy selling near the downtrend line as seen from the long wick on the candlestick. The bears will now again try to pull the price below $30 and extend the decline to $26.\par \par \uc2 If bulls want to invalidate this \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view, they will have to quickly push the SOL/USDT pair above the downtrend line. That could clear the path for a possible rally to $35.50 and thereafter to $39 where the bears may again offer a strong resistance.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) rebounded off the strong support near $0.06 on Oct. 13, indicating that the bulls are defending the level aggressively. Buyers are trying to propel the price above the moving averages on Oct. 14.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/354ca7f7-6f40-4b3a-a623-e28a6836a241.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they manage to do that, the DOGE/USDT pair could rise to $0.07. This level is again likely to act as a strong resistance but if bulls push the price above it, the pair could attempt a rally to the overhead level of $0.09.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if the price turns down from the moving averages, the bears will again attempt to sink the price below the support near $0.06. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because if it cracks, the pair could retest the June low near $0.05.\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT\par \par \uc2 The long tail on Polygon\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) Oct. 13 candlestick shows that bulls are aggressively buying near the $0.71 to $0.69 support zone. Buyers continued their momentum on Oct. 14 and tried to push the price above the downtrend line but the bears held their ground.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/a5d52ff2-480e-477b-bb5b-7184542322b4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The flattish moving averages and the RSI near the midpoint suggest a balance between supply and demand. This equilibrium could tilt in favor of the buyers if the price rises above the downtrend line. The MATIC/USDT pair could then rise to $0.86 and if this level is crossed, the next stop could be $0.94.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price reverses direction from the downtrend line, it will show that bears continue to sell on rallies. The pair could then remain stuck between the downtrend line and the support at $0.69.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph.com. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMTAvMzcxMzJkOTYtZDM2NC00NmI2LTlkOWEtMGRiNWRlYmYyMzQwLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020221014eiae000e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
