ings to know in Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) this week and altcoins analysis.\par \par \uc2 To kick things off, we broke down the latest news in the markets this week.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-sheds-1k-in-3-minutes-as-us-cpi-inflation-overshoots"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin price sheds $1K in 3 minutes}}}\uc2  as U.S. CPI inflation overshoots. Bitcoin's 4% losses swiftly ensue as inflation fails to cool as quickly as hoped for, resulting in a wave of sell-offs for the crypto market. We do a deep dive into what the data means and the implications on the wider market. Does this mark the end of the recent price pump we saw earlier this week or will we rebound once things settle down? We take a look at what President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had to say about the latest CPI data and also what Crypto \uc2 Twitter\uc2  is discussing about the matter. Lots to unpack here so make sure you stay tuned as we break down the information for you.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/the-fed-the-merge-and-22k-btc-5-things-to-know-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Fed, the Merge and $22K BTC}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 5 things to know in Bitcoin this week. A \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  weekly close sees Bitcoin tackle realized price while analysts speculate on major \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming days. With the new CPI data causing the price of Bitcoin to fall, can the Merge bring some relief to the markets or will it cause further downside? We also do a deep dive into the Ethereum Merge and explain why it is such a significant event in crypto's history and why you should be keeping a close eye on the developments. We also highlight certain scams you need to be aware of to keep yourself safe.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/price-analysis-9-12-btc-eth-bnb-xrp-ada-sol-doge-dot-matic-shib"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis: \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , SOL, and MATIC.}}}\uc2  Our experts take a look at a few altcoins that have been making some interesting moves this week. They analyze the charts and make a case for where the price could possibly go. So make sure you stick around because you don't want to miss this vital information.\par \par \uc2 Next up is a new segment called \u8220\'20\'1CQuick Crypto Tips,\u8221\'20\'1D which aims to give newcomers to the crypto industry quick and easy tips to get the most out of their experience. This week\u8217\'20\'19s tip: Trade, do not gamble.\par \par \uc2 Market expert Marcel Pechman then carefully examines the Bitcoin and Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) markets. Are the current market conditions \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  or \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? What is the outlook for the next few months? Pechman is here to break it down. The experts also go over some market news to bring you up to date on the latest regarding the top two cryptocurrencies.\par \par \uc2 Lastly, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got insights from Cointelegraph Markets Pro, a platform for crypto traders who want to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.cointelegraph.com/?via=news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stay}}}\uc2  one step ahead of the market. The analysts use Cointelegraph Markets Pro to identify three altcoins that stood out this week: \uc2 Audius\uc2 's token AUDIO, Ocean Protocol's token OCEAN and DIGG's token DIGG.\par \par \uc2 Do you have a question about a coin or topic not covered here? Don\u8217\'20\'19t worry. Join the \uc2 YouTube\uc2  chat room, and write your questions there. The person with the most interesting comment or question will be given a $50 gift voucher to the Cointelegraph merch store.\par \par \uc2 The Market Report streams live every Tuesday at 12:00 pm ET (4:00 pm UTC), so be sure to head on over to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/user/cointelegraph"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph\u8217\'20\'19s YouTube page}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/user/cointelegraph"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 smash}}}\uc2  those like and subscribe buttons for all our future videos and updates.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDkvNmJjZDYzZDYtOTNlZS00ODExLTgyMTAtMjBhOGVkYzA4OGVmLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220913ei9d000ba\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Crypto traders eye ATOM, APE, CHZ and QNT as Bitcoin flashes bottom signs\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,792 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 September 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin, ATOM, APE, CHZ and QNT are facing resistance at higher levels, but the chart patterns suggest that the current recovery may extend for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 The United States equities markets rallied sharply last week, ending a three-week losing streak. The S&P 500 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/09/08/stock-market-futures-open-to-close-news.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rose}}}\uc2  3.65% last week while the Nasdaq Composite soared 4.14%. Continuing its close correlation with the U.S. equities markets, Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) also made a strong comeback and is trying to end the week with gains of more than 7%.\par \par \uc2 The sharp rally in the stock markets and cryptocurrency markets are showing signs of a bottoming formation but it may be too early to predict the start of a new bull move. The equities markets may remain on the edge before the release of the U.S. inflation data on Sept. 13 and the Federal Reserve meeting on Sept. 20-21.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/e03a312c-fff8-404f-8f81-25540fc16654.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto market data daily view. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Along with taking cues from the equities markets, the cryptocurrency space has its own important events to look forward to. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-ready-for-the-merge-as-last-shadow-fork-completes-successfully"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Both the Ethereum\u8217\'20\'19s Merge}}}\uc2  and Cardano\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cardano-ada-eyes-15-rally-despite-charles-hoskinson-s-fear-over-macro-factors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vasil hard fork}}}\uc2  scheduled in the next few days could heighten \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  in several cryptocurrencies.\par \par \uc2 Although choppy markets increase the risk, they may offer short-term trading opportunities to nimble traders. Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of five cryptocurrencies that look interesting in the near term.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin soared above the 20-day exponential moving average ($20,662) on Sept. 9, which was the first indication that the selling pressure could be reducing. The bears are attempting to stall the recovery at the 50-day simple moving average ($21,946) but a positive sign is that the bulls have not given up much ground.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/f7e23b76-8c6f-4db0-b45c-3f85d97551af.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to slope up gradually and the relative strength index (RSI) is in the positive territory indicating that the path of least resistance is to the upside. If bulls propel the price above the 50-day SMA, the BTC/USDT pair could rally toward the stiff overhead resistance at $25,211. The bears are expected to defend this level with vigor.\par \par \uc2 Another possibility is that the price turns down from the 50-day SMA. If that happens, the pair may drop to the 20-day EMA. This is an important level to keep an eye on because a break and close below it could open the doors for a drop to $18,626. Alternatively, if the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA, it will increase the likelihood of a break above the 50-day SMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/5a278dcb-17c4-483e-afb7-a30a6f90f51c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT 4-hour chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The pair picked up momentum after rising above the breakdown level of $19,520. The sharp rally pushed the RSI into the overbought territory, suggesting a minor consolidation or correction. Buyers are facing a stiff challenge near $22,000 but they have not ceded ground to the bears. This suggests that every minor dip is being purchased.\par \par \uc2 If bulls propel the price above $22,000, the pair could quickly rally toward $23,500 where the bears may again attempt to stall the up-move.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down and breaks below the 20-EMA, the pair could drop to $20,576. A break below this level will suggest that the pair may consolidate in a large range between $22,000 and $18,626 for some time.\par \par \uc2 ATOM/USDT\par \par \uc2 Cosmos ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/cosmos-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM}}}\uc2  ) broke above the overhead resistance of $13.45 on Sept. 8, indicating demand at higher levels. The next stiff resistance is at $20.30 which leaves room for a rally.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/ceb9ee30-03ef-44ff-b03e-e8c504634aee.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ATOM/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 However, before that, the bears will try to pull the price below the breakout level of $13.45. This is an important level to keep an eye on because a break and close below it will indicate that the recent breakout may have been a bull trap.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price turns up from the current level or rebounds off $13.45, it will suggest that bulls are in control and are buying on every dip. If bulls thrust the price above $17.20, the up-move may pick up momentum and reach $20.30.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/470a496b-d12b-4ab6-9023-2a9f57e6b716.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ATOM/USDT 4-hour chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the ATOM/USDT pair surged after breaking above the overhead resistance at $13.45. That pushed the RSI deep into the overbought territory and started a correction but a positive sign is that the bulls have not given up much ground.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the current level, the possibility of a break above $17.20 increases. If that happens, the up-move may continue and the pair may rally toward $20.30.\par \par \uc2 This positive view could invalidate in the near term if the price continues lower and plummets below the 20-EMA. If that happens, the pair could decline to the 50% Fibonacci retracement level of $14.36.\par \par \uc2 APE/USDT\par \par \uc2 ApeCoin (APE) rebounded strongly off the support at $4.17, indicating aggressive buying at lower levels. This suggests that the corrective phase could be ending, making it an interesting candidate for the short term.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/e6505552-abe5-434b-bd1f-57dc96038838.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 APE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Buyers pushed the price above the 20-day EMA ($5) on Sept. 9 and the APE/USDT pair formed an inside-day Doji candlestick pattern on Sept. 10. This uncertainty resolved to the upside on Sept. 11 with a strong rally to the 50-day SMA ($5.85). The bears may try to stall the recovery at this level.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the current level but rebounds off the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the sentiment has turned positive and traders are buying on dips. The bulls will then again attempt to drive the price above the 50-day SMA. If they do that, the pair could soar toward the overhead resistance at $7.80.\par \par \uc2 This positive view could invalidate in the near term if the price turns down and breaks below the 20-day EMA. In that case, the pair may drop to $4.17.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/e0d81c4f-ae75-4a82-8499-e650cd139b96.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 APE/USDT 4-hour chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-EMA on the 4-hour chart has started to turn up and the RSI has risen into the overbought territory. This indicates that bulls have the upper hand but a short-term pullback is possible.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the current level but rebounds off $5.30, it will suggest strong demand at lower levels. The bulls will then make another attempt to push the price above $5.83 and extend the recovery to $6.44.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down and breaks below the 20-EMA, the advantage may tilt in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/terra-back-from-the-dead-luna-price-rises-300-in-september"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Terra back from the dead? LUNA price rises 300% in September}}}\par \par \uc2 CHZ/USDT\par \par \uc2 Chiliz (CHZ) broke above the 20-day EMA ($0.20) on Sept. 9, which was the first indication that the corrective phase may be ending. Hence, this token made it to the list.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/7ec1dbd7-7a03-4d2f-97ac-c5d1135a990f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 CHZ/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears tried to pull the price back below the 20-day EMA on Sept. 10 but the bulls have held their ground. Buyers are attempting to push the price toward the overhead resistance at $0.26 but the up-move may face strong headwinds near $0.23.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down but does not fall below the 20-day EMA, it will increase the likelihood of a rally to $0.26. Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down and breaks below $0.20, it will suggest that bears are active at higher levels. That could pull the price to the 50-day SMA ($0.18).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/1b3fd424-a3ca-422f-9060-5bbca9965668.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 CHZ/USDT 4-hour chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the bears are defending the downtrend line. If the price turns down from the current level but rebounds off the moving averages, it will suggest that bulls are attempting a comeback.\par \par \uc2 Buyers will then again attempt to drive the price above the downtrend line. If they succeed, the pair may start its northward march toward $0.23 and later to $0.26.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price plummets below $0.20, it will suggest that the pair may remain inside the falling wedge pattern. That could pull the price down to $0.18.\par \par \uc2 QNT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Quant ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/quant-network"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 QNT}}}\uc2  ) did not break below the strong support at $87.60, indicating that the sentiment is positive and bulls are buying on dips. That is the reason for its selection.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/e70ff933-c230-41ac-8d92-db65b9521255.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 QNT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The sharp rebound off $87.60 broke above the 20-day EMA ($100) on Sept. 8, which was the first indication that the corrective phase may be ending. The bears posed a strong challenge near the 50-day SMA ($105) but could not sink the price back below the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 This indicated that the sentiment had turned positive and the bulls are buying on dips. Buyers pushed the QNT/USDT pair above the 50-day SMA on Sept. 11. If bulls sustain the higher levels, the pair could rise to $117 and then to $124. A break above this level could open the doors for a rally to $130.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view could be invalidated if the price turns down and breaks below the 20-day EMA. If that happens, the pair could drop to the strong support at $87.60.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/ace924bd-9f17-47b3-8c76-4208eb74aa5d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 QNT/USDT 4-hour chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the pair rebounded sharply off the support at $87.60. The bears posed a strong challenge near $108 but a positive sign is that the bulls purchased the dip to the 20-EMA. This indicates that traders are viewing dips as a buying opportunity.\par \par \uc2 Buyers resumed the recovery by pushing the price above the overhead resistance at $108. The pair could rally to $113 and later to $117. Conversely, if the price turns down and plummets below the 20-EMA, the pair could drop to the 50-SMA.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDkvZDU0MmU3ZmMtMWZlMS00MmU0LWFiNTAtYWFmNTYyYWQyZjhmLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220911ei9b000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 9/7: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, DOGE, DOT, MATIC, SHIB\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,871 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 September 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and altcoins have dropped to critical support levels. The rebound strlacks strength, increasing the risk of further downside.\par \par \uc2 After trading near the $20,000 level for several days, Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) turned down sharply and dropped below $19,000 on Sept. 6. The fall was not limited to the cryptocurrency markets as the United States equities markets also closed lower on Sept. 6.\par \par \uc2 Risky assets have been facing selling pressure in the past few days as investors are worried that the Federal Reserve could continue with its aggressive tightening policy.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 CME\uc2  FedWatch Tool {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cmegroup.com/trading/interest-rates/countdown-to-fomc.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shows}}}\uc2  that the probability for a 75 basis point rate hike in the September meeting has risen to 80% from 69% a week back. This {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/traders-say-bitcoin-price-bounce-is-overdue-after-a-massive-btc-long-position-appears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extended the rise in the U.S. dollar index}}}\uc2  (DXY), which closed above 110 on Sept. 6.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. equities markets and the cryptocurrency markets are attempting a relief rally on Sept. 7 but the recovery is likely to sustain only after the DXY shows signs of topping out.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/528c3b22-e896-45b3-a61f-6cfba94e2074.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Although the bear market has been brutal, it is an encouraging sign to see that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/vcs-pour-14-2b-into-crypto-in-h1-2022-but-investments-now-slowing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 venture capital firms have continued to plow money}}}\uc2  into cryptocurrency and blockchain companies. According to a \uc2 KPMG\uc2  report released on Sept. 6, the total investments in the first half of 2022 by these firms hit $14.2 billion, which comes after the record $32.1 billion investments made in 2021.\par \par \uc2 What are the critical overhead resistances in Bitcoin and altcoins that need to be crossed for the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum to pick up? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s tight range trading between $19,520 and $20,576 resolved to the downside on Sept. 6. The bears pulled the price to the strong support zone between $18,910 and $18,626.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/174ff5fe-506a-4890-b84f-25987c4b40e5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the zone, the BTC/USDT pair could rally to the breakdown level of $19,520. The bears will attempt to flip this level into resistance. If they manage to do that, the likelihood of a break below the support zone increases.\par \par \uc2 That could sink the pair to the vital support at $17,622. A break and close below this level could signal the resumption of the downtrend. The downsloping 20-day exponential moving average (EMA)($20,427) and the relative strength index (RSI) near the oversold territory indicate that bears are in control.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of strength will be a break and close above the 20-day EMA. Such a move will indicate that bulls are attempting a comeback.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) rose above the moving averages on Sept. 6 but the bulls could not clear the overhead hurdle at $1,700. The bears sold aggressively and pulled the price back below the 20-day EMA ($1,597).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/4b14af0d-5e12-4424-8a2f-cd39143c46e8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will try to build upon the advantage and sink the price below the neckline of the head and shoulders (H&S) pattern. If they succeed, the ETH/USDT pair could drop to $1,422 and then to the important support at $1,280. The pattern target of this \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup is $1,050.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price bounces off the neckline, it will suggest that bulls continue to view dips as a buying opportunity. The pair could then consolidate between the neckline and $1,700 for some time. A break and close above $1,700 could clear the path for a possible rally to $2,030.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  turned down sharply from the 20-day EMA ($282) on Sept. 6 and broke below the critical support at $275. This completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  H&S pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/c21fa388-ab1c-4e6d-abc0-84a1705abbb3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Generally, after the breakdown from a major support, the price returns to retest the level. In this case, buyers will try to push the price back above $275. If they manage to do that, several aggressive bears may get trapped. That could result in a short squeeze and the BNB/USDT pair could rally to $308.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price turns down from $275, it will suggest that bears have flipped the level into resistance. That could start a decline to $240 and if this support also gives way, the next stop could be the pattern target at $212.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  above the overhead resistance at $0.34 on Sept. 6 but the bears trapped the aggressive buyers and pulled the price below the immediate support at $0.32.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/043e4614-3d9c-44de-a5b8-7c5c0277c720.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A minor positive is that the bulls have not allowed the price to sustain below $0.32. The long tail on the Sept. 7 candlestick shows buying at lower levels. If the price sustains above $0.32, the XRP/USDT pair could extend its range-bound action for some more time.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level and sustains below $0.32, it will clear the path for a possible decline to $0.30. The bulls are likely to defend this level with all their might.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) closed above the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) (0.49) on Sept. 4 and the bulls defended the level on Sept. 5. Buyers tried to extend the relief rally on Sept. 6 but met with a wall of selling near $0.51.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/dc46bee8-c84c-48fd-8503-46f21ecd9ef5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price turned down sharply and broke below the moving averages. Both moving averages are flattish and the RSI is just below the midpoint, indicating a range-bound action in the near term. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could oscillate between $0.44 and $0.51 in the next few days.\par \par \uc2 The bears will have to sink the price below $0.44 to open the doors for a drop to the crucial support at $0.40. Alternatively, if the price turns up from the current level and breaks above $0.51, the pair could rally to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) rallied to the 20-day EMA ($33) on Sept. 6 but the bulls could not overcome this barrier. This suggests that the sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/9c2ff401-06bb-43d0-96dc-f7d2d786b79f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A minor positive is that the bulls have not allowed the price to dip below the immediate support at $30. If the price turns up from the current level, the bulls will again try to drive the SOL/USDT pair above the 20-day EMA. If they succeed, the pair could rally to the 50-day SMA ($38).\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns down and breaks below $30, the pair could extend its slide to the vital support at $26. The bulls are likely to mount a strong defense at this level because if this support cracks, the pair could resume its downtrend.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls attempted to push Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($0.06) on Sept. 6 but the bears sold the rally aggressively and pulled the price below the immediate support at $0.06.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/4a0f79a0-db94-4c84-96b2-8775cbd4735a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Buyers are attempting to push the price back above $0.06 on Sept. 7. If they succeed, the DOGE/USDT pair could again rally to the overhead resistance at the 20-day EMA. This remains a critical level to watch out for in the near term because a rally above it could push the price to $0.07.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from $0.06 or the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that bears are selling on rallies. That could increase the possibility of a drop to the strong support at $0.05.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-hits-10-week-low-amid-painful-us-dollar-rally-warning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin price hits 10-week low amid 'painful' US dollar rally warning}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Buyers attempted to push Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) above the moving averages on Sept. 5 and 6 but the bears defended the level aggressively as seen from the long wick on the candlesticks.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/066b7952-6b1c-4e40-8d0d-3ec27b3bb554.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($7.38) is sloping down and the RSI is in the negative territory, indicating advantage to sellers. If bears sink and sustain the price below the immediate support at $6.79, the DOT/USDT pair could slip to the crucial support at $6. The bulls are likely to mount a strong defense at this level.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns up from the current level and rises above the moving averages, it will suggest strong buying on dips. That could push the pair to $9.17 and later to the overhead resistance at $10.\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Buyers defended the 50-day SMA ($0.87) on Sept. 5 and attempted to extend the recovery on Sept. 6 but the bears had other plans. They sold aggressively at $0.92 and pulled Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) back below the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/e6cd09c2-bf9a-46d6-b72e-d40c1e3d8233.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.85) has started to turn down and the RSI is near 46, indicating that bears have a slight edge. Sellers will attempt to pull the price to the strong support at $0.75.\par \par \uc2 This is an important support to watch out for because a break and close below it could complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  H&S pattern. If that happens, the MATIC/USDT pair could start a decline to $0.63 and thereafter to the pattern target of $0.45.\par \par \uc2 This negative view could invalidate in the near term if bulls push the pair above $0.93. The price could then rise to the strong overhead resistance at $1.05.\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls purchased the dip in Shiba Inu ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/shiba-inu-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SHIB}}}\uc2  ) on Sept. 5 but they could not sustain the price above the 20-day EMA ($0.000013). This indicates that bears are selling on every minor rally.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/558caad7-3e9a-4f13-af19-f1c1f904c202.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has turned down and the RSI is just below the midpoint, indicating a minor advantage to bears. The sellers will attempt to sink the price to the psychological support at $0.000010 and then to $0.000009. Buyers are expected to defend this support zone with vigor.\par \par \uc2 Another possibility is that the price turns up from the current level and breaks above the moving averages. Such a move will suggest that selling dries up at lower levels. The SHIB/USDT pair could first rise to $0.000015 and later to $0.000018.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDkvZTFmZjczMWMtODI2My00ZTVhLTg3MGEtYjI1YTMwM2VjZTcyLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220907ei97000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 9/5: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 SOL\uc2 , DOGE, DOT, MATIC, SHIB\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,819 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 September 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and altcoins are holding their immediate support levels, but traders are searching for a trigger to push the market higher.\par \par \uc2 The cryptocurrency markets have been quiet over the weekend. The sideways price action continues on Sept. 5 and there are unlikely to be any fresh triggers from the United States equities markets, which are closed for Labor Day.\par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  picture for cryptocurrencies looks clouded as the energy crisis in Europe sent the euro to a two-decade low versus the U.S. dollar. Meanwhile, the U.S. dollar index (DXY) which has an inverse correlation with the equities markets and cryptocurrencies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-sees-new-20k-showdown-5-things-to-know-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soared above 110 for the first time}}}\uc2  since June 2002.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/2bf1911f-36d6-4343-a56c-5af93fd8a289.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 A positive sign among all the mayhem is that Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) has not given up much ground over the past few days and continues to trade near the psychological level of $20,000. This suggests that traders are not panicking and dumping their positions in a hurry.\par \par \uc2 Could bulls push and sustain Bitcoin above $20,000 and will this trigger buying in altcoins? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has been stuck inside a tight range between $19,520 and $20,576 for the past few days. This indicates indecision among the bulls and the bears. Although bulls are buying the dips, they have failed to clear the overhead resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/c6165c56-b0b3-4b3b-b5d5-aadf82f7d376.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($20,775) and the relative strength index (RSI) in the negative territory increase the likelihood of a break below $19,520. If that happens, the BTC/USDT pair could drop to the strong support zone between $18,910 and $18,626.\par \par \uc2 Buyers are expected to defend this zone with all their might. If the rebound breaks above the 20-day EMA, the pair could rise to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($22,253). The bulls will have to clear this hurdle to open the doors for a possible rally to $25,211.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if bears sink the price below $18,626, the pair could retest the final support at $17,622. A break below this support could signal the resumption of the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) has been stuck between the 20-day EMA ($1,605) and the neckline of the head and shoulders (H&S) pattern since Aug. 31 but this tight-range trading is unlikely to continue for long.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/19c48df7-4a8a-4e14-b123-eb987f871e1d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If buyers push and sustain the price above the 20-day EMA, the ETH/USDT pair could rally to the overhead resistance at $1,700. This is an important level to keep an eye on because a break and close above it could signal that bulls are back in control. The pair could then rally to $2,030 and later to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated in the near term if the price turns down from the moving averages and breaks below $1,422. If that happens, the pair could slide to $1,280. The bulls are expected to defend this level with vigor but if the bears overpower them, the decline could extend to the pattern target of $1,050.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  has been trading near the strong support of $275 for the past few days but the bulls have not been able to achieve a strong rebound off it. This indicates a lack of demand at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/d766f6fb-ec2f-46ca-a3b9-08c0f51c2131.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($286) has been sloping down and the RSI is below 41, indicating that bears have the upper hand. If the price breaks and closes below $275, the BNB/USDT pair will complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  head and shoulders pattern. The pair could then start its decline to $240 and later to the pattern target of $212.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns up from the current level and breaks above the moving averages, it will suggest that bulls are back in the game. The pair could then rise to the overhead resistance at $308.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) has been stuck between $0.32 and $0.34 for the past few days but this tight range trading is unlikely to continue for long.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/c60c4c4a-69b4-467b-b4ad-f1d43b9dacfa.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will attempt to sink the price below $0.32. If they succeed, the XRP/USDT pair could extend its decline to the crucial support at $0.30. Buyers are likely to defend this level aggressively as they had done on three previous occasions.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price rebounds off $0.32 and breaks above $0.34, it will suggest a short-term advantage to the bulls. The pair could then rise to the 50-day SMA ($0.36) and later to the stiff overhead resistance at $0.39.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) broke and closed above the 50-day SMA ($0.49) on Sept. 4 but the bulls could not sustain the breakout. This suggests that bears continue to sell on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/e78909c2-924b-44c4-84fe-0673b9a907cd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price turned down and broke below the 50-day SMA on Sept. 5, indicating that bears are attempting to trap the aggressive bulls. If the price dips below the 20-day EMA ($0.47), the pair could drop to $0.44 and later to $0.42.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA and rises above $0.51, it will suggest a change in sentiment from selling on rallies to buying on dips. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could then rise to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) has been trading near $32 for the past few days but a negative sign is that buyers have not been able to push and sustain the price above it.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/9a68741d-0ca5-4ded-9828-7d92112319c2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down and slips below $30, the \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT pair could decline to the vital support at $26. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because if this support gives way, the pair could start the next leg of the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 In the near term, if buyers push the price above the 20-day EMA ($34), it will suggest that the selling pressure could be reducing. The pair could then attempt a rally to the 50-day SMA ($38) where the bears may again pose a strong challenge.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) has stayed above the immediate support at $0.06 for the past few days but the bulls have failed to achieve a strong rebound off it. This indicates that demand dries up at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/84a578b1-5d37-4dfc-b197-ef166d333d56.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A tight consolidation near a support usually results in a breakdown. The downsloping 20-day EMA ($0.06) and the RSI in the negative zone indicate the path of least resistance is to the downside. If bears sink and sustain the price below $0.06, the DOGE/USDT pair could drop to the crucial support at $0.05.\par \par \uc2 To invalidate this negative view, buyers will have to push and sustain the pair above $0.07. If they manage to do that, the pair could rise toward the overhead resistance at $0.09.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/eth-merge-coingecko-co-founder-shares-strategy-for-forked-tokens"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH Merge: CoinGecko co-founder shares strategy for forked tokens}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) remains stuck inside a large range between $6 and $10 for the past several days. The price has gradually been inching higher and the bulls are attempting to clear the overhead hurdle at the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/75ddd00b-adcf-46ff-99a7-4017100429bd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they manage to do that, it will suggest that lower levels continue to attract buyers. The DOT/USDT pair could then attempt a rally to $9.17 and later to the overhead resistance at $10.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price fails to rise above the moving averages, it will suggest that bears are active at higher levels. The sellers will then attempt to sink the price below the strong support at $6.79. If that happens, the pair could drop to the crucial support at $6, which is likely to attract strong buying.\par \par \uc2 The price action inside a large range is usually random and volatile. Hence, it is difficult to project the short-term price moves inside the range with certainty.\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) has been range-bound between $1.05 and $0.75 for the past several days. Although bulls pushed the price above the 50-day SMA ($0.88) on Sept. 1, they have not been able to build upon this strength. This indicates that demand dries up at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/875c1262-9b17-4014-b7d6-c60140ae712e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will attempt to sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($0.85). If they succeed, the MATIC/USDT pair could drop toward the strong support at $0.75.\par \par \uc2 This is an important level for the bulls to defend because a break and close below it could complete a head and shoulders pattern. The pair could then start a correction to $0.63 and later to the pattern target at $0.45.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price rebounds off the moving averages and rises above $0.91, the likelihood of a rally to $1.05 increases. The bears are expected to pose a stiff resistance at this level.\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Buyers pushed Shiba Inu ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/shiba-inu-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SHIB}}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($0.000013) on Sept. 4 but the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick shows that bears are selling at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/faa12a0e-34e6-46a7-87a8-ad63b71da848.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price turned down and slipped below the moving averages on Sept. 5. The bears will now try to sink the SHIB/USDT pair to $0.000012, which is likely to attract buyers. The 20-day EMA is flattening out and the RSI is just below the midpoint, indicating a balance between buyers and sellers.\par \par \uc2 This balance could tilt in favor of the bears if they pull the price below $0.000012. The pair could then decline to $0.000010. Alternatively, if bulls drive and sustain the price above $0.000014, the pair could attempt a rally to $0.000018.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDkvNzZjMDI5M2YtMzQ2My00ZTAyLWI5ZGYtM2UzY2JmMWE3MzdhLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220905ei95000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 9/2: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, DOGE, DOT, MATIC, SHIB\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,853 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and select altcoins face selling at higher levels \u8212\'20\'14 proof that \b \highlight22\uc2 investor sentiment\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains negative as traders sell on rallies.\par \par \uc2 Nonfarm payrolls rose by 315,000 jobs in August, down from the July increase of 526,000 jobs. The report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/09/02/august-2022-jobs-report-.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was}}}\uc2  just below the Dow Jones estimate of 318,000 jobs and the slowest monthly gain since April 2021. The S&P 500 rose in response to the report, but later erased its gains, indicating that bears continue to sell on rallies.\par \par \uc2 That may be because the U.S. dollar index (DXY), which had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-dollar-smashes-yet-another-20-year-high-as-bitcoin-price-sags-2-7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retreated from its Sept.1 20-year high}}}\uc2 , recovered part of its losses. The bears will have to pull the DXY lower to boost the prices of stocks and thcryptocurrency markets as both are usually inversely correlated with the dollar index.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/544745ec-14fe-4844-a1b9-8b9c549097dd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Although Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) has dropped more than 70% from its all-time high of $69,000, several traders have held on to their position. Data from trading analysis platform TipRanks shows that 62% of wallets have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/62-of-wallets-did-not-sell-bitcoin-for-a-year-amid-the-bear-market-data"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held Bitcoin for a year or more}}}\uc2 . The number of wallets holding Bitcoin for less than a month is only 6%. This suggests that investors are taking a long-term approach and holding on to their positions.\par \par \uc2 Could bulls push Bitcoin and altcoins above the overhead resistance levels? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin broke and closed above the downtrend line on Sept. 1, which is the first indication that the short-term corrective phase could be ending.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/89ee1432-0e42-4bf5-bd5f-9467eea031b2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 There is a minor resistance at $20,576 but if bulls thrust the price above it, the BTC/USDT pair could reach the 20-day (EMA)exponential moving average ($21,091).\par \par \uc2 This is an important level to watch out for because if buyers clear this hurdle, it will suggest that the negative sentiment could be weakening. The BTC/USDT pair could then attempt a rally to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA)($22,318).\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from $20,576 or the 20-day EMA, the bears will make one more attempt to sink the pair to the critical support zone of $18,910 to $18,626. The bulls are expected to defend this zone aggressively.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 20-day EMA ($1,61) on Aug. 31 but a positive sign is that the bulls did not allow the price to dip below the neckline of the head and shoulders (H&S) pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/dbac0a2c-5dc8-48db-bdce-0b3656a577ea.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price bounced off the neckline on Sept. 1 and has risen to the 50-day SMA ($1,640). The bears will try to defend the zone between the 50-day SMA and $1,700 but if bulls overcome this barrier, the ETH/USDT pair could pick up momentum. The pair could then rise to $1,848 and later retest the stiff resistance at $2,030.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from the overhead zone, the pair could again drop to the neckline. If this support breaks down, the pair could drop to $1,422 and then to $1,280. Although the pattern target of a breakdown from the H&S setup is $1,050, the bulls are likely to defend the support at $1,280 vigorously.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 20-day EMA ($289) on Aug. 31 and slipped below the strong support at $275 on Sept. 1. However, the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick shows aggressive buying at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/da3f4737-4e3e-49ab-8df0-179be9a4ab31.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will again attempt to push the price above the 20-day EMA. If they manage to do that, it will be the first sign that the bears may be losing their grip. The BNB/USDT pair could then rally to $308 where the bears may again mount a strong defense.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the current level or the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the sentiment remains negative and bears are selling on minor rallies.\par \par \uc2 That will increase the possibility of a break below the support at $275. If that happens, the pair will complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  H&S pattern. The pair could then slide to $240 and later to the pattern target at $212.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  has been trading between $0.32 and $0.34 since Aug. 28. This tight range trading indicates indecision among the bulls and the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/aa8ee151-d752-4b81-bbf7-9fdaa0eeb852.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA ($0.34) and the RSI below 39 suggest that bears have the upper hand. If the price turns down and breaks below $0.32, the XRP/USDT pair could drop to the important support at $0.30. If this level also gives way, the pair could start the next leg of the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 This negative view could invalidate in the near term if bulls drive the price above the 20-day EMA. The pair could then rise to the 50-day SMA ($0.36). Such a move will suggest that the pair may continue to consolidate between $0.30 and $0.39 for some more time.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has been trading close to the 20-day EMA ($0.47) for the past three days but the bulls have failed to push the price above it. This suggests that the bears are defending the 20-day EMA but a minor positive is that the bulls have not given up much ground.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/5c384e3a-c8c8-4623-b4d0-ceebd07390a1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the 20-day EMA and breaks below $0.44, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could drop to $0.42. This level may again act as a strong support but if bears sink the price below it, the pair could decline to $0.40.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price breaks above the 20-day EMA, the pair could rise to the 50-day SMA ($0.49). The bulls will have to overcome this barrier to clear the path for a possible rally to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) has been stuck in a tight range between $30 and $33 since Aug. 27, which indicates indecision among buyers and sellers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/47d8f0fa-f96f-4fff-a9db-0d61fccc2f83.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA ($34) and the RSI in the negative territory indicate advantage to bears. If sellers sink the price below $30, the SOL/USDT pair could drop to the crucial support at $26. This is an important level to keep an eye on because a break and close below it could signal the resumption of the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns up from the current level and breaks above the 20-day EMA, the pair could rise to the 50-day SMA ($39). Such a move could suggest that the pair may remain stuck between $30 and $48 for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) once again bounced off the strong support at $0.06 on Sept. 1 but the rebound lacks strength. This suggests the absence of aggressive buying at these levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/b796d8f2-1657-4cc3-8d7b-6de97f1f2496.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA ($0.07) and the RSI in the negative territory indicate advantage to sellers. If the price turns down from the current level or the 20-day EMA, the bears will again attempt to sink the DOGE/USDT pair below $0.06. If they succeed, the pair could slide to the vital support at $0.05.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will invalidate in the short-term if bulls drive the price above the moving averages. If that happens, the pair could attempt a rally to the overhead resistance at $0.09.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cel-climbs-50-as-celsius-network-aims-to-return-50m-to-clients"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CEL climbs 50% as Celsius Network aims to return $50M to clients}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) had been stuck inside a tight range between $7.38 and $6.79 for the past few days, indicating indecision among the bulls and the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/55b87616-db27-4fd1-9fcf-685661308d2e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This balance could tilt in favor of the buyers if they push and sustain the price above the overhead zone between $7.38 and the 50-day SMA ($7.87). The DOT/USDT pair could then start a rally to $9.17 and later to the overhead resistance at $10.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the overhead zone, it will suggest that the sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on rallies. The bears will have to sink the price below $6.79 to gain the upper hand. The pair could then decline to the crucial support at $6.\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) broke and closed above the moving averages on Sept. 1. This opens the doors for a possible rally to the overhead resistance at $1.05. The bears are likely to defend this level aggressively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/f5fdc1ba-7580-4a8a-afb0-a8cc7187a092.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from $1.05, the MATIC/USDT pair could extend its range-bound action for some more time.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.84) is flat but the RSI has jumped into the positive territory, indicating that the momentum favors the buyers. If bulls thrust the price above $1.05, the pair could extend its up-move to $1.19.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down and breaks below the 20-day EMA, the pair could again drop to $0.75. A break below this support could sink the pair to $0.63.\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Shiba Inu ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/shiba-inu-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SHIB}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 20-day EMA ($0.000013) on Aug. 30 and dropped to the important support at $0.000012. This suggests that bears are active at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/c1d956fe-3b8f-4245-a9db-81a8df0bdb12.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A minor positive is that the bulls did not allow the price to sustain below $0.000012 on Sept.1. The price remains stuck between the 20-day EMA and the $0.000012 support.\par \par \uc2 If bulls drive the price above the 20-day EMA, the SHIB/USDT pair could rally to the overhead resistance at $0.000014. This level may again act as a stiff hurdle but if bulls overcome it, the rally could extend to $0.000018.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price once again turns down from the moving averages and breaks below $0.000012, the pair could decline to $0.000010.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDkvNGFkNmQ3MjktMDM5Mi00NTc4LWE2MzYtNWFkMjEwZWJhNjIwLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220902ei92000e5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 8/31: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 SOL\uc2 , DOGE, DOT, MATIC, SHIB\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,776 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 August 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s technical setup leans toward an additional downside, leading some traders to exit altcoins.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) price has been trying to change course while the S&P 500 is still giving up gains on a daily basis. Even though the United States equities markets have been grinding lower since Aug. 26, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-clings-to-20k-as-analyst-says-fed-buried-soft-landing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin has managed to hold on}}}\uc2  to the $20,000 mark.\par \par \uc2 However, investor interest seems to be shifting away from Bitcoin. That has led to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/eth-products-grow-in-august-as-btc-products-dip-cryptocompare-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reduction in assets under management}}}\uc2  (AUM) for Bitcoin investment products, which dropped 7.16% in August to $17.4 billion, according to a new report by CryptoCompare.\par \par \uc2 In comparison, the AUM for Ethereum products increased 2.36% to $6.81 billion during the same period, indicating that investors are positioning themselves in Ethereum products ahead of the Merge.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-08/7cb9b5e7-41ed-4756-9197-8aa5db88f370.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Even though prices are down across the ecosystem, bear markets at least offer attractive opportunities to long-term investors. To capitalize on this opportunity, \uc2 Reddit\uc2  co-founder \uc2 Alexis Ohanian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s venture capital firm Seven Seven Six is aiming to raise $177.6 million for a crypto investment fund. On similar lines, former executives from \uc2 Galaxy Digital\uc2  and Genesis are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/everything-s-on-sale-reddit-founder-galaxy-and-genesis-execs-raise-big-money"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 looking to raise a $500 million fund}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although the near term looks uncertain, long-term investors may be looking for bottom fishing opportunities. Could Bitcoin and major altcoins stay above their immediate support levels? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin turned down from the downtrend line on Aug. 30 but a minor positive is that the bulls purchased the dip near $19,500. The bulls are again trying to push the price above the downtrend line on Aug. 31.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-08/375aafbd-0b01-486a-9032-a385cddd8a57.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the BTC/USDT pair could rally to the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($21,325), which is an important level to keep an eye on. If the price turns down from this level, the bears will attempt to pull the pair to the strong support zone of $18,910 to $18,626. A break and close below this zone could open the doors for a retest of the critical support at $17,622.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if bulls push the price above the 20-day EMA, the pair could rise to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($22,333). If bulls clear this hurdle, the pair could pick up momentum and rally toward the overhead resistance at $25,211. The bulls have to overcome this barrier to indicate that the bottom may be in place.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) turned up from $1,422 on Aug. 29 and climbed back above the neckline of the head and shoulders pattern. This suggests that the breakdown on Aug. 26 may have been a bear trap.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-08/03bc51a1-4a90-4cb7-8cd0-c7e3d461c387.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls are attempting to push the price above the moving averages. If they succeed, the ETH/USDT pair could rise to the overhead resistance at $1,700. This is an important level to keep an eye on because a break and close above it could open the doors for a possible rally to $2,000.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the price turns down from the overhead resistance and breaks below $1,422. Such a move will suggest that the recovery may be over. The pair could then decline to $1,280 and later to $1,050.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  bounced off the strong support at $275 on Aug. 29, indicating that the bulls are defending this level aggressively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-08/b707706f-dd86-4ee9-95d1-4225a71b2bbe.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls attempted to push the price above the 20-day EMA ($292) on Aug. 30 and 31 but the bears held their ground. If the price breaks and closes below the $275 support, the BNB/USDT pair will complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  head and shoulders pattern. That could start a decline to $240 and later to the pattern target at $212.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price rebounds off $275 and breaks above the 20-day EMA, the pair could rise to $308. A break and close above this resistance could clear the path for a rally to $338.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Buyers have been defending the $0.32 level for the past three days but have failed to achieve a strong rebound. This suggests a lack of demand for Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-08/c3ff7adc-aca4-424d-991b-8981d5219d79.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA ($0.34) and the relative strength index (RSI) in the negative territory indicate that bears have a slight edge. If the price turns down from the current level or the 20-day EMA and breaks below $0.32, the XRP/USDT pair could slide to the vital support at $0.30.\par \par \uc2 The bulls are expected to defend this level with all their might because a break below this support could signal the resumption of the downtrend. Conversely, if bulls drive the price above the moving averages, the pair may rally to $0.39.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) bounced off $0.42 on Aug. 29 and reached the 20-day EMA ($0.47) where the bears are mounting a stiff resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-08/ef85b56a-f365-43ed-b1d8-9f71b9d0d52f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the current level, it will suggest that bears continue to sell on minor rallies. The bears will then try to sink the price to the crucial support at $0.40. This is an important level to keep an eye on because a break and close below it could signal the start of the next leg of the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if buyers thrust the price above the moving averages, it will suggest strong demand at lower levels. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could then rally to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) rebounded off $30 and rose above the $32 level on Aug. 29 but the bears again pulled the price back below the level on Aug. 30. This suggests that bears are selling on every minor rise.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-08/7221c0b5-1107-48d3-8b03-77f20fafd3eb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls are again trying to push the price to the 20-day EMA ($35), which is an important level to watch out for in the short term. If bulls drive the price above this level, the \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT pair could rise to the 50-day SMA ($39).\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the negative territory indicate advantage to sellers. If the price turns down from the current level or the 20-day EMA and breaks below $30, the pair could drop to the crucial support at $26.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls successfully defended the support at $0.06 in the past few days but have failed to achieve a strong rebound off it. This suggests a lack of demand for Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-08/2ad71283-913d-4679-8ea9-fca8d178496c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A tight consolidation near a strong support increases the possibility of a breakdown. If that happens, the DOGE/USDT pair could start its downward move toward the June 18 low near $0.05. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because a break and close below it could resume the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rises from the current level and breaks above the moving averages, it will suggest that the latest leg of the corrective phase may be over. The pair could then attempt a rally to $0.09.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/potential-bitcoin-price-double-bottom-could-spark-btc-rally-to-30k-despite-extreme-fear"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Potential Bitcoin price double-bottom could spark BTC rally to $30K despite \u8216\'20\'18extreme fear\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) has been trading below the moving averages since Aug. 19 but the bears have not been able to sink the price to the strong support at $6. This suggests that selling dries up at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-08/89a88140-7677-4522-b484-1166c7f209ed.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will again try to push the price above the moving averages. If they succeed, it will suggest that the DOT/USDT pair could rally to $9.17 and then to the overhead resistance at $10. The bears are likely to mount a strong defense at this level.\par \par \uc2 Another possibility is that the price turns down from the moving averages and breaks below $6.79. If that happens, the bears will try to sink the pair to the crucial support of $6. A break and close below this level could indicate the resumption of the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) rebounded off the $0.75 support on Aug. 29 and reached the 20-day EMA ($0.83) on Aug. 30 but the Doji candlestick pattern indicates indecision among buyers and sellers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-08/33b1cbf3-0c02-4a54-bb0e-a8090977885a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bulls drive and sustain the price above the moving averages, the MATIC/USDT pair could start its northward march toward the overhead resistance at $1.05. This level is again likely to face stiff resistance from the bears.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the moving averages, it will suggest that bears are defending the level vigorously. The pair could then again decline toward the strong support of $0.75. If this support cracks, the pair could drop to $0.63.\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Shiba Inu ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/shiba-inu-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SHIB}}}\uc2  ) climbed back above the important level of $0.000012 on Aug. 29, indicating that bulls are buying on dips. Buyers tried to push the price above the 20-day EMA ($0.000013) on Aug. 30 but the bears did not relent.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-08/dc0f625b-5251-4d01-8468-b135f7f94fd9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price is stuck between the 20-day EMA and $0.000012. This tight-range trading is unlikely to continue for long. If bears sink and sustain the price below $0.000012, the SHIB/USDT pair could drop to $0.000010.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price breaks above the 20-day EMA, the pair could rally to the overhead resistance at $0.000014. The bulls have to overcome this barrier to open the doors for a poss