\par\par \b \uc2 Cryptocurrency Bear Market Opportunities: Cardano ( \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 ), Solana (SOL), and Degrain (DGRN)\b0\par\par\uc2 Crypto Daily \par \uc2 628 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 July 2022\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2022, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 The overlapping factors responsible for creating a bear market can rarely be predicted.\par \par \uc2 A case study would be Bitcoin (BTC) which obtained an all-time high of $69,000 and then slumped recently to a $18,000 low. Declines like that, in any cryptocurrency, can prove damaging to investments if resources are not channeled to alternative profitable cryptocurrencies and opportunities. Here, we have explored three potentially profitable investment opportunities to enable you to stay afloat in the cryptocurrency bear market.\par \par \uc2 Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) - one to watch\par \par \uc2 Among cryptocurrencies that share a record of dropping in value recently, Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) stands out with a promise of growth assured via analytical predictions.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the native token of the Cardano network, currently holds a market value below $0.50 and an all-time high of $3.10. It is built on proof-of-stake technology rather than algorithmic methods reducing gas fees and runs an average of 250 transactions per second far exceeding the Ethereum network with speed.\par \par \uc2 With such innovations and phase-based implementations,Cardano, (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is speculated by several crypto-enthusiasts and analysts to rise to figures ranging from $0.97 to $49.98 before 2030. With a market cap of $15.78 billion, and \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  down 75% from its all time high, it presents room for growth and returns on investment.\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) - is recovery on the cards?\par \par \uc2 The Solana Ecosystem is one of the fastest, most accessible and more popular networks in the cryptocurrency space. With an all-time high of $260.06 and a recorded low of $0.5052, Solana (SOL) stands as a crypto asset that has performed arguably well, although concerns regarding centralization have had a ripple effect on the coin. Predictions state that recent GameFi collaborations will boost the performance of the Solana token (SOL).\par \par \uc2 With a market cap of $12.3 billion and a current token value of $35.18, the coin is predicted by experts to reach between $44.91 - $56.39 if it continues a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend.\par \par \uc2 Degrain (DRGN) - high potential investment opportunity\par \par \uc2 With a promise of inclusivity and decentralization, Degrain plans to restructure the trend and is capitalizing on limitations within the existing NFT industry.\par \par \uc2 It aims to be the world's first NFT marketplace to enable cross-chain exchange for traders and NFT creators in the marketplace. It has identified the lack of real world utility as one of the limitations of current NFT platforms and intends to work with real world companies whilst distributing this revenue to investors and stakers of its token, DGRN. It has just launched its presale on July 7th, with 11 million tokens sold in 60 seconds, causing a number of crypto analysts to take notice.\par \par \uc2 As an investment option, it offers the perfect opportunity within the cryptocurrency bear market as the platform encourages users to trade, offers a safer and more decentralized pathway, and also helps users generate massive ROI. Using the native token, DRGN, Degrain could accelerate the upward trend in exchange and volume sales of NFT.\par \par \uc2 Presently in its early days, analysts expect an increase of 5000% before September 30th 2022 when the pre-sale ends. It is a rare opportunity to invest in a project with so much potential. With the current token price of $0.01, it is a strong contender to be one of the greatest investment opportunities of 2022.\par \par \uc2 Website: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://degrain.io"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://degrain.io}}}\par \par \uc2 Presale: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://presale.degrain.io"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://presale.degrain.io}}}\par \par \uc2 Telegram: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.me/degrainio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.me/degrainio}}}\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/degrainio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/degrainio}}}\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This is a sponsored press release, and is for informational purposes only. It does not reflect the views of Crypto Daily, nor is it intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, or financial advice\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020220712ei7c000gp\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 7/11: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, DOGE, DOT, SHIB, AVAX\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,808 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 July 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and select altcoins are discounted and trading close to critical support levels, but will buyers step in?\par \par \uc2 The United States dollar index (DXY) resumed its strong uptrend on July 11, indicating that investors are preparing for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-inflation-data-will-be-messy-5-things-to-know-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13 CPI report to be hotter than expected.}}}\uc2  A survey of economists by \uc2 Bloomberg{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bnnbloomberg.ca/inflation-expectations-three-years-out-ease-to-3-6-ny-fed-survey-shows-1.1790410"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimates}}}\uc2  that in June consumer prices surged to 8.8%, a four-decade high.\par \par \uc2 Arthur Hayes, the former CEO of derivatives trading platform BitMEX, believes that the U.S. dollar and the euro were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-risks-new-lows-as-20k-looms-amid-dollar-euro-parity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moving towards hitting parity}}}\uc2 . If that happens, the central banks will have to adopt yield curve control, which could lead to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-for-beginners/what-is-the-purpose-of-bitcoin-speculation-or-dollarization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disintegration of the currency and ultimately benefit Bitcoin}}}\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/c2411103-3d46-476f-bbed-8eba25fd3edc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Glassnode analyst James Check said in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/despite-worst-bear-market-ever-bitcoin-has-become-more-resilient-glassnode-analyst-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview with Cointelegraph}}}\uc2  that the number of Bitcoin holders is higher during the current bear market. This shows the resilience of the Bitcoin network. Another positive is that the smaller investors have used the dip to add to their positions.\par \par \uc2 Although the short-term picture remains skewed to the downside, the long-term view looks encouraging for bulls. Will Bitcoin and the altcoins attract buying at lower levels? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin turned down from $22,527 on July 8 and broke below the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($21,164) on July 10. This suggests that traders who may have bought at lower levels booked profits and the aggressive bears initiated short positions.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/711062df-457d-429b-9551-2f2c06d2b4ae.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The BTC/USDT pair could decline to the support line of the triangle. This is an important level to watch out for because a bounce off it will suggest that the bulls are accumulating near this level. The buyers will then again try to clear the overhead hurdle at the 20-day EMA and push the pair to $23,363.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($24,496) will suggest that the pair may have bottomed out.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price breaks below the support line, it will indicate that bears are in control. The sellers will then attempt to sink the pair to the strong support zone between $18,626 and $17,622.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the overhead resistance at $1,280 on July 8, suggesting that the bears are defending the level aggressively. The sellers pulled the price below the 20-day EMA ($1,192) on July 10 and are attempting to break the support line of the triangle on July 11.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/5b863781-55e5-4481-b04e-bd8011a97930.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they manage to do that, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup will be invalidated. That could sink the ETH/USDT pair to $998. This is an important level to watch out for because a break and close below it could result in a retest of $881.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price rebounds off the support line, it will suggest that the bulls are accumulating on dips. The buyers will have to push and sustain the price above $1,280 to gain the upper hand in the near term. The pair could then rise to the 50-day SMA ($1,422) and later rally to the pattern target at $1,679.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  failure to rise to the 50-day SMA ($257) may have attracted profit-booking from short-term traders. That has pulled the price below the 20-day EMA ($234).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/ca454862-fa74-4af4-99ed-60abdbd27197.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains below the 20-day EMA, the BNB/USDT pair could once again drop to the strong support at $211. This is an important level to keep an eye on because a strong bounce off it will indicate accumulation on dips.\par \par \uc2 The bulls will then make another attempt to push the price above the 50-day SMA. If they succeed, it will signal that the pair may have bottomed out. This positive view could invalidate if the price breaks below $211.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) failed to rise above the resistance line of the symmetrical triangle on July 8, indicating that the bears are selling on rallies. Strong selling on July 10 pulled the price to the support line of the triangle.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/24ced71d-65b7-4425-af29-09a61839213d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The relative strength index (RSI) has dropped near 43 indicating that the momentum favors the bears. If sellers sink the price below the support line, the XRP/USDT pair could decline to $0.30 and then retest the critical support at $0.28. If this level cracks, the pair could resume its downtrend.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the support line, it will suggest that the bulls continue to buy on dips. The buyers will then make another attempt to push the price above the triangle and gain the upper hand. If that happens, the pair could rise to $0.41.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) failure to sustain above the 20-day EMA ($0.47) suggests that the bears are defending this level aggressively. The sellers have pulled the price to the immediate support at $0.44.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/2829086d-4f57-412c-bce8-8605f4cf69b2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The gradually downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the negative territory suggest that bears have a slight edge. If the sellers pull the price below $0.44, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could retest the crucial support at $0.40. If this level gives way, the selling could intensify and the pair may resume its downtrend.\par \par \uc2 The bulls are expected to defend the zone between $0.40 and $0.44 with vigor. If the price rebounds off this zone with strength, the buyers will again attempt to clear the overhead hurdle at the moving averages.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) broke below the 20-day EMA ($36) on July 11 and has dropped to the support line of the symmetrical triangle pattern. The price is reaching close to the apex of the triangle, indicating the possibility of a breakout within the next few days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/9763ffc9-eba8-4d93-b810-a5107c57fe20.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price drops below the support line, it will indicate that the uncertainty has resolved in favor of the bears. The SOL/USDT pair could then drop to $31 and later to the critical support at $26. A break below this support could signal the resumption of the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rises from the current level, it will suggest that the bulls are attempting to defend the support line. The pair could then rise to the resistance line. The bulls will have to clear this hurdle to start an up-move to $50.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 50-day SMA ($0.07) on July 8 and broke below the 20-day EMA ($0.07) on July 10. The bears are attempting to sink the price below the strong support at $0.06.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/43016422-4f76-4bf7-b1d1-34da7e522da5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the DOGE/USDT pair could slide to the crucial support at $0.05. A break and close below this level could signal the start of the next leg of the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rebounds off $0.06, it will suggest buying at lower levels. The bulls will then make another attempt to clear the hurdle at the 50-day SMA and push the pair to $0.08. The next trending move could begin on a break above $0.08 or below $0.06. Until then, random range-bound action is likely to continue.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/3-reasons-why-solana-can-repeat-ethereum-s-2018-fractal-to-5-000-gains"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3 reasons why Solana can repeat Ethereum's 2018 fractal to 5,000% gains}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) turned down from $7.30 on July 10 after bulls repeatedly failed to push the price above the resistance. The bears will attempt to sink the price to the strong support at $6.36.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/07e63a92-db7e-4297-abea-003da0075342.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Although the downsloping moving averages indicate advantage to bears, the positive divergence on the RSI suggests that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could be weakening. The longer the price remains stuck between $6.36 and $7.30, the stronger will be the breakout from it.\par \par \uc2 If bears sink the price below $6.36, the DOT/USDT pair could resume the downtrend. The pair could then drop to $5. Conversely, if the price rises from the current level and breaks above $7.30, the pair could rally to the 50-day SMA ($8.20). A break and close above this level could suggest that the downtrend could be over.\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Shiba Inu ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/shiba-inu-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SHIB}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the overhead resistance at $0.000012 on July 10, indicating that bears are active at higher levels. The sellers will try to pull the price to $0.000010.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/2c67c5ef-ba2e-4eca-b7a9-fff46306f0af.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off this level with strength, it will suggest demand at lower levels. The bulls will then again attempt to drive the price above the overhead resistance at $0.000012. If they succeed, the SHIB/USDT pair could rally to $0.000014.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price rebounds off $0.000010 but fails to climb above $0.000012, then it will point to a consolidation in the near term. The bears may gain the upper hand if the price slips below $0.000010. The pair could then decline to $0.000009.\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the overhead resistance at $21.35 on July 8, indicating that bears continue to defend the level aggressively. The bears are attempting to extend their short-term advantage by pulling the price below the 20-day EMA ($18.83).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/079d2edb-92bb-4901-8822-483a64aebc60.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they manage to do that, the AVAX/USDT pair could remain stuck inside the range between $13.71 and $21.35. The flattish 20-day EMA and the RSI near 46 also point to a possible consolidation in the short term.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of strength will be a break and close above $21.35. Such a move could signal the start of a new up-move. The pair could then rally to $29 where the bears may again mount a strong resistance.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDcvMTc0NmYwZmYtZjhkNi00OGRiLTkyZjItYjc2ZjI1MDI4NDUxLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220711ei7b000e1\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Michael Saylor\par \b \uc2 BTC bull \uc2 Michael Saylor\uc2 : Ethereum is \u8216\'20\'18obviously\u8217\'20\'19 a security\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Brian Quarmby \par \uc2 640 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 July 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Commenting on other competing assets to ETH such as \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Michael Saylor\uc2  noted \u8220\'20\'1CI think all of the proof-of-stake networks are securities and they\u8217\'20\'19re all very risky [...]\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2  CEO and Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) bull \uc2 Michael Saylor\uc2  said that Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) is \u8216\'20\'18obviously\u8217\'20\'19 a security as he doubled down on labeling BTC as the only commodity in the crypto sector.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Altcoin Daily, Saylor was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JGvdMWvyRAA&t=0s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 questioned}}}\uc2  on his take regarding the classification of both {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/gillibrand-and-lummis-state-that-most-altcoins-are-securities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC and ETH as commodities}}}\uc2  by United States Senators such as Kirsten Gillibrand and Cynthia Lummis, along with figureheads from the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) and the \uc2 Commodities Futures Trading Commission (CFTC)\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Saylor provided a lengthy run down on what he thou are the fundamental differences between the Bitcoin and Ethereum networks, as he suggested that only the former has remained unchanged over the years:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think Ethereum is a security, I think it\u8217\'20\'19s pretty obvious, [...] it was issued by an ICO, theres a management team, there was a pre-mine, there\u8217\'20\'19s a hard fork, there\u8217\'20\'19s continual hard forks, there\u8217\'20\'19s a difficulty bomb that keeps getting pushed back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The CEO argued that the constant need for software upgrades on a network driven by a team or entity represents an indicator that ETH is a security. He pointed to the design of the long-delayed difficulty bomb, which he said will \u8220\'20\'1Cmurder\u8221\'20\'1D the entire ETH mining industry as an example of such.\par \par \uc2 According to Saylor, for a \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be classified as a commodity, it needs to be backed by a \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely decentralized protocol where nobody can change it even if they wanted to change it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor it to be a commodity there can\u8217\'20\'19t be an issuer, and the truth is you can\u8217\'20\'19t really make decisions. I mean one of the fundamental insights in the crypto industry is that the fact that you can change it, is what makes it a security,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Securities are generally understood as fungible and tradable financial instruments that are used to raise capital in public or private markets. While commodities are seen as goods or assets that have a monetary utility. Assets like gold and silver are seen as hard commodities, while soft commodities are goods such as rice or tea.\par \par \uc2 Saylor reiterated that BTC is a commodity as the core of the Bitcoin network cannot be altered, much like the physical makeup of gold:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you want to establish yourself as a digital commodity, then you\u8217\'20\'19re trying to create something like gold in cyberspace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite Saylor\u8217\'20\'19s arguments, however, the Bitcoin network has seen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-for-beginners/what-is-the-lightning-network-in-bitcoin-and-how-does-it-work"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 multiple network upgrade}}}\uc2  s over the years. The most notable one in recent history was the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/breaking-the-bitcoin-network-welcomes-taproot-soft-fork-upgrade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taproot soft fork}}}\uc2  from November 2021, which aimed to improve Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s scripting capabilities and privacy.\par \par \uc2 Asked about his thoughts on other altcoins such as Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Saylor once again echoed his maximalist sentiments, stating:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think all of the proof-of-stake networks are securities and they\u8217\'20\'19re all very risky [...] it\u8217\'20\'19s above my pay grade, the regulators will decide whether or not they allow them to continue or nor noth they don't allow them to continue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-cheap-at-20k-as-btc-price-to-wallet-ratio-mimics-2013"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin 'cheap' at $20K as BTC price to wallet ratio mimics 2013}}}\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2  went on to note that one of the major reasons he favors BTC over all other crypto assets is that he holds concerns over altcoins being non-compliant security tokens that could get regulated out of existence.\par \par \uc2 Saylor\u8217\'20\'19s MicroStrategy has continued to snap up BTC despite the tanking value of the asset in 2022, and as of June 29, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/microstrategy-scoops-up-480-bitcoin-amid-market-slump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 firm held 129,699 BTC}}}\uc2  worth around $3.98 billion at the time.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDcvZmExMTM0NDEtMDcxMC00ZTRiLWEzYTEtOTRhZTVkYmUwMGFlLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220711ei7a00033\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Michael Saylor\par \b \uc2 BTC bull \uc2 Michael Saylor\uc2 : Ethereum is 'obviously' a security\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Brian Quarmby \par \uc2 642 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 July 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Commenting on other competing assets to ETH such as \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Michael Saylor\uc2  noted \u8220\'20\'1CI think all of the proof-of-stake networks are securities and they\u8217\'20\'19re all very risky [...]\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2  CEO and Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) bull \uc2 Michael Saylor\uc2  said that Ethereum ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) is \u8216\'20\'18obviously\u8217\'20\'19 a security as he doubled down on labeling BTC as the only commodity in the crypto sector.\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JGvdMWvyRAA&t=0s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  with Altcoin Daily, Saylor was questioned on his take regarding the classification of both {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/gillibrand-and-lummis-state-that-most-altcoins-are-securities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC and ETH as commodities}}}\uc2  by U.S. Senators such as Kirsten Gillibrand and Cynthia Lummis, along with figureheads from the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) and the \uc2 Commodities Futures Trading Commission (CFTC)\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Saylor provided a lengthy run down on what he thou are the fundamental differences between the Bitcoin and Ethereum networks, as he suggested that only the former has remained unchanged over the years:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think Ethereum is a security, I think it\u8217\'20\'19s pretty obvious, [...] it was issued by an ICO, theres a management team, there was a pre-mine, there\u8217\'20\'19s a hard fork, there\u8217\'20\'19s continual hard forks, there\u8217\'20\'19s a difficulty bomb that keeps getting pushed back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The CEO argued that the constant need for software upgrades on a network driven by a team or entity represents an indicator that ETH is a security. He pointed to the design of the long-delayed difficulty bomb, which he said will \u8220\'20\'1Cmurder\u8221\'20\'1D the entire ETH mining industry as examples of such.\par \par \uc2 According to Saylor, for a \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be classified as a commodity, it needs to be backed by a \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely decentralized protocol where nobody can change it even if they wanted to change it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor it to be a commodity there can\u8217\'20\'19t be an issuer, and the truth is you can\u8217\'20\'19t really make decisions. I mean one of the fundamental insights in the crypto industry is that the fact that you can change it, is what makes it a security,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Securities are generally understood as fungible and tradable financial instruments that are used to raise capital in public or private markets. While commodities are seen as goods or assets that have a monetary utility. Assets like gold and silver are seen as hard commodities, while soft commodities are goods such as rice or tea.\par \par \uc2 Saylor reiterated that BTC is a commodity as the core of the Bitcoin network cannot be altered, much like the physical makeup of gold:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you want to establish yourself as a digital commodity, then you\u8217\'20\'19re trying to create something like gold in cyberspace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite Saylor\u8217\'20\'19s arguments, however, the Bitcoin network has seen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-for-beginners/what-is-the-lightning-network-in-bitcoin-and-how-does-it-work"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 multiple network upgrade}}}\uc2  s over the years. The most notable one in recent history was the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/breaking-the-bitcoin-network-welcomes-taproot-soft-fork-upgrade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taproot soft fork}}}\uc2  from November 2021, which aimed to improve Bitcoin's scripting capabilities and privacy.\par \par \uc2 Asked about his thoughts on other altcoins such as Cardano\u8217\'20\'19s native token \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Saylor once again echoed his maximalist sentiments, stating:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think all of the proof-of-stake networks are securities and they\u8217\'20\'19re all very risky [...] it\u8217\'20\'19s above my pay grade, the regulators will decide whether or not they allow them to continue or nor noth they don't allow them to continue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-cheap-at-20k-as-btc-price-to-wallet-ratio-mimics-2013"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin 'cheap' at $20K as BTC price to wallet ratio mimics 2013}}}\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2  went on to note that one of the major reasons he favors BTC over all other crypto assets is that he holds concerns over altcoins being non-compliant security tokens that could get regulated out of existence.\par \par \uc2 Saylor\u8217\'20\'19s MicroStrategy has continued to snap up BTC despite the tanking value of the asset in 2022, and as of June 29, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/microstrategy-scoops-up-480-bitcoin-amid-market-slump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 firm held 129,699 BTC}}}\uc2  worth around $3.98 billion at the time.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDcvZmExMTM0NDEtMDcxMC00ZTRiLWEzYTEtOTRhZTVkYmUwMGFlLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220710ei7a0005m\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 7/8: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, DOGE, DOT, SHIB, AVAX\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,767 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 July 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and select major altcoins have risen from their recent lows, signaling an increase in \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-surges-to-21-8k-but-analysts-warn-that-the-move-could-be-a-fakeout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rallied to the 200-week moving average}}}\uc2  on July 8, a level that could act as a battleground between the bulls and the bears. Several analysts are watching this level because a break and close above it could be the first sign that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/trading-for-beginners/bull-vs-bear-crypto-market-what-is-the-difference-and-how-to-handle-both"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the bear market may be ending}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  senior commodity strategist \uc2 Mike McGlone\uc2  said that Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s 50-week and 100-week moving averages are showing similar signs as made before the 2018 bear market bottom. Therefore, McGlone expects Bitcoin to give a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bloomberg-analyst-tips-bullish-btc-recovery-in-next-six-months"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strong rebound in the second half}}}\uc2  of 2022.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/36bcdaf0-f2c9-4aa4-b0a0-36d0e93708b4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Another positive sign is that Bitcoin rose above $22,000 on July 8 even as the United States dollar index (DXY) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-builds-best-weekly-candle-since-march-despite-new-dxy-peak"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continued its northward march}}}\uc2 . This suggests that the strong inverse correlation between Bitcoin and the DXY may be starting to weaken.\par \par \uc2 Could Bitcoin extend its recovery pulling the crypto markets higher? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin broke above the resistance line of the symmetrical triangle and the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($21,233) on July 7, indicating that bulls are making a comeback.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/d574b56a-6626-4e1e-b3b0-debb4178bd3f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The flattening 20-day EMA and the relative strength index (RSI) just below the midpoint suggest that the selling pressure may be reducing.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the current level or the breakout level from the triangle, it will suggest that the sentiment has turned positive and traders are buying the dips. That could increase the possibility of a rally to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($25,015) and then to the pattern target at $26,490.\par \par \uc2 This positive view could invalidate in the short term if the price breaks back below the 20-day EMA and re-enters the triangle. That will indicate aggressive selling by the bears at higher levels. The pair could then drop to the support line of the triangle.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) broke above the 20-day EMA ($1,198) on July 7 and reached the overhead resistance at $1,280 on July 8. The bears are defending this resistance aggressively and are attempting to sink the price back below the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/43e12042-b6ef-4e57-843f-bd2bdc55cfad.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they do that, the ETH/USDT pair could drop to the support line of the ascending triangle. This is an important level to keep an eye on because a break and close below it could invalidate the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup. That could pull the price down toward the critical support at $881.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA and breaks above $1,280, it will complete the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  ascending triangle pattern. The pair could then rise to the 50-day SMA ($1,470) and later rally to the pattern target at $1,679.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  broke and closed above the 20-day EMA ($233) on July 6 but the bulls are struggling to push the price to the 50-day SMA ($262). This suggests that bears are active at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/b8542db9-e661-44c2-b1e7-f86c9fca56ff.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The sellers are trying to pull the price back below the 20-day EMA. If they can pull it off, the BNB/USDT pair could slide to the strong support at $211.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the sentiment is turning positive and the bulls are buying on dips. The bulls will then attempt to drive the price above the 50-day SMA and gain control. That could clear the path for a possible rally to $300.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) attempted a break above the resistance line of the symmetrical triangle but the bears had other plans. They aggressively defended the level and are trying to sink the price back below the 20-day EMA ($0.33).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/b6975473-8494-49c1-8999-8cf30eeb2b6b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the XRP/USDT pair could extend its stay inside the triangle for some more time. The flattish 20-day EMA and the RSI near the midpoint do not give a clear advantage either to buyers or sellers.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above the triangle could indicate the start of a new up-move. The pair could then rally to the pattern target at $0.48. Alternatively, a break below the triangle could open the doors for a retest at $0.28.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) rose above the 20-day EMA ($0.47) on July 8 but the bulls could not sustain the higher levels. This indicates that the bears are aggressively defending the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/b90a6a33-d440-4cc4-a3c5-5830481e8994.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The sellers will attempt to build upon their advantage by pulling the price below the strong support at $0.44. If they manage to do that, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could drop to the important level at $0.40. A break and close below this support could indicate the start of the next leg of the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 To invalidate this \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view, buyers will have to push and sustain the price above the 50-day SMA ($0.51). If they manage to do that, the pair could rally to $0.60 and then to $0.70.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 The buyers attempted to push Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) above the 50-day SMA ($38.79) on July 5 and 6 but could not overcome the barrier. This suggests that the bears are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/5419064c-9e04-4346-8370-a8675aa7dc94.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price is getting squeezed inside a symmetrical triangle. This points to a possible range expansion in the short term. If the price turns down and breaks below the triangle, the SOL/USDT pair could slide toward the critical support at $26.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns up and breaks above the resistance line of the triangle, it will suggest that bulls have the upper hand. The pair could then rally to the psychological level of $50 where the bears may again mount a strong defense.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) attempted a break above the 50-day SMA ($0.07) on July 8 but the bears did not relent. The sellers are trying to use the opportunity to sink the price back below the 20-day EMA ($0.07).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/3356f768-4724-43e5-92a6-5bf07bbb26bb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The RSI is near the midpoint and the 20-day EMA has flattened out, suggesting a balance between buyers and sellers. This equilibrium could tilt in favor of the bulls if they push and sustain the price above the 50-day SMA. Such a move could clear the path for a rally to $0.08 and next to $0.09.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down and breaks below $0.06, the bears will strive to pull the DOT/USDT pair to the vital support at $0.05.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/doge-days-of-summer-shiba-inu-gains-40-on-dogecoin-two-months-after-record-lows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE days of summer: Shiba Inu gains 40% on Dogecoin two months after record lows}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) attempted to break above the overhead resistance at the 20-day EMA ($7.38) on July 7 but the bears held their ground. This indicates that bears are active at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/c007acf7-60c0-45c6-b183-c1a4db4d20cf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will attempt to pull the price toward the critical support at $6.36. This is an important support for the bulls to watch out for because a break and close below it could indicate the resumption of the downtrend. The DOT/USDT pair could then decline to the psychological level of $5.\par \par \uc2 This negative view could invalidate if the price turns up and rises above the 20-day EMA. If that happens, the pair could attempt a rally to the 50-day SMA ($8.38). This level may again act as a resistance but if bulls clear this hurdle, it may signal a potential change in trend.\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT\par \par \uc2 The tight range trading in Shiba Inu ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/shiba-inu-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SHIB}}}\uc2  ) resolved to the upside on July 7 as the price broke above the immediate resistance at $0.000011. The bears tried to sink the price back below $0.000011 on July 8 but the long tail on the candlestick indicates strong buying on dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/8e5f70ad-96ea-44b0-b895-619e126c3c9f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The buyers will attempt to push the price above the stiff resistance at $0.000012. If they succeed, it will indicate demand at higher levels. The SHIB/USDT pair could then rally to $0.000014 where the bears may again pose a strong challenge.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the current level and sustains below $0.000011, it will suggest that the breakout on July 7 may have been a bull trap. The bears will then try to pull the price back below the critical support at $0.000010. If that happens, the next stop could be $0.000009.\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) has been trading between $13.71 and $21.35 for the past few days, indicating a bottoming formation. The 20-day EMA ($18.78) has flattened out and the RSI is just above the midpoint, indicating a balance between the bulls and the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/d8f4a398-58d0-42b6-b280-4304910ad223.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If buyers drive the price above the overhead resistance at $21.35, it will signal the start of a new up-move. The AVAX/USDT pair could rally to the pattern target of $29 where the bears may again mount a strong resistance. If the price turns down from this level but does not drop below $21.35, it will suggest that a bottom may have been made at $13.71.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below the 20-day EMA, it will indicate that the range-bound action may continue for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDcvMGVjYWMzYzctYzY3OS00NDk4LWEzYzctMTUwYzM1NmJmOTI0LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220708ei78000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Short Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Institutional investors shorting Bitcoin made up 80% of weekly inflows\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Brian Quarmby \par \uc2 452 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 July 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Short BTC products have now seen year-to-date inflows totaling $77.2 million, with that figure placing it behind only multi-asset products and SOL products.\par \par \uc2 Institutional investors loaded up on a record $51.4 million worth of investment products offering exposure to shorting the price of Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) last week.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blog.coinshares.com/volume-87-digital-asset-fund-flows-weekly-report-ef9a4c955c32"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According}}}\uc2  to data from the latest edition of \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 weekly \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows\u8221\'20\'1D report, there was $64 million worth of inflows for \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  products between June 27 and July 1, with short BTC funds representing 80% of that figure.\par \par \uc2 United States-based investors accounted for the lion\u8217\'20\'19s share of inflows at $46.2 million, with short-BTC investment products in solid demand after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/proshares-will-launch-etf-aimed-at-shorting-bitcoin-following-dip-under-20k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/proshares-will-launch-etf-aimed-at-shorting-bitcoin-following-dip-under-20k}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/proshares-will-launch-etf-aimed-at-shorting-bitcoin-following-dip-under-20k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProShares launched the first-ever}}}\uc2  U.S.-based short Bitcoin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-for-beginners/bitcoin-etfs-a-beginners-guide-to-exchange-traded-funds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exchange-traded fund (ETF)}}}\uc2  on June 22. The ETF trades under the ticker BITI and offers shorting exposure via futures contracts:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis highlights investors are adding to long positions at current prices, with the inflows into short-Bitcoin possibly due to first-time accessibility in the US rather than renewed negative sentiment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  also noted that institutional investors from Brazil, Canada, Germany and Switzerland snapped up a combined $20 million worth of crypto investment products. Sweden partially offset that figure with $1.8 million worth of outflows.\par \par \uc2 Short BTC products have now seen year-to-date inflows totaling $77.2 million, with that figure placing it behind only multi-asset products and Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) products, which have posted $213.5 million and $110.3 worth of inflows so far in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Looking at the inflows for other \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  products, those offering exposure to Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) generated $4.9 million, marking the second consecutive week of inflows after a lengthy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/almost-100m-exits-us-crypto-funds-in-anticipation-of-hawkish-monetary-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 11-week trend of shedding}}}\uc2 . However, year-to-date ETH funds are still down with $450.9 million worth of outflows.\par \par \uc2 The remainder of the inflows was spread across multi-asset funds at $4.4 million, while SOL, Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and BTC products also posted minor inflows of $1 million, $700,000, $600,000, and $600,000, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/coinshares-acquires-french-crypto-asset-manager-napoleon-am"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CoinShares acquires French crypto asset manager Napoleon AM}}}\par \par \uc2 The surge in short BTC fund inflows last week also follows from the prior week when there was $423 million worth of outflows for \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  products, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-crypto-asset-products-saw-record-weekly-outflows-of-423m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highest amount ever on CoinShares\u8217\'20\'19 records}}}\uc2 . Notably, short BTC funds escaped the carnage that week, posting $15.3 million worth of inflows, while BTC products saw significant outflows of $453 million.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDcvNGI4MDkxNjMtMzA4My00MGUxLTlhM2EtMjRlOWY2YjRiMWI4LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220705ei750002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Short Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Institutional investors shorting Bitcoin made up 80% of weekly inflows\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Brian Quarmby \par \uc2 437 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 July 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Short BTC products have now seen year-to-date inflows totaling $77.2 million, with that figure placing it behind only multi-asset products and Solana (SOL) products.\par \par \uc2 Institutional investors loaded up on a record $51.4 million worth of investment products offering exposure to shorting the price of Bitcoin (BTC) last week.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blog.coinshares.com/volume-87-digital-asset-fund-flows-weekly-report-ef9a4c955c32"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  from the latest edition of \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 weekly \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows\u8221\'20\'1D report, there was $64 million worth of inflows for \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  products between June 27 and July 1, with short BTC funds representing 80% of that figure.\par \par \uc2 U.S.-based investors accounted for the lion's share of inflows at $46.2 million, with short-BTC investment products in solid demand after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/proshares-will-launch-etf-aimed-at-shorting-bitcoin-following-dip-under-20k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProShares launched}}}\uc2  the first-ever U.S.-based short Bitcoin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-for-beginners/bitcoin-etfs-a-beginners-guide-to-exchange-traded-funds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exchange-traded fund}}}\uc2  (ETF) on June 22. The ETF trades under the ticker BITI and offers shorting exposure via futures contracts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis highlights investors are adding to long positions at current prices, with the inflows into short-Bitcoin possibly due to first-time accessibility in the US rather than renewed negative sentiment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  also noted that institutional investors from Brazil, Canada, Germany, and Switzerland snapped up a combined $20 million worth of crypto investment products. Sweden partially offset that figure with $1.8 million worth of outflows.\par \par \uc2 Short BTC products have now seen year-to-date inflows totaling $77.2 million, with that figure placing it behind only multi-asset products and Solana (SOL) products, which have posted $213.5 million and $110.3 worth of inflows so far in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Looking at the inflows for other \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  products, those offering exposure to Ether (ETH) generated $4.9 million, marking the second consecutive week of inflows after a lengthy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/almost-100m-exits-us-crypto-funds-in-anticipation-of-hawkish-monetary-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 11-week trend of shedding}}}\uc2 . However, year-to-date ETH funds are still down with $450.9 million worth of outflows.\par \par \uc2 The remainder of the inflows was spread across multi-asset funds at $4.4 million, while SOL, Polkadot (DOT), Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), and BTC products also posted minor inflows of $1 million, $700,000, $600,000, and $600,000 respectively.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/coinshares-acquires-french-crypto-asset-manager-napoleon-am"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CoinShares acquires French crypto asset manager Napoleon AM}}}\par \par \uc2 The surge in short BTC fund inflows last week also follows from the prior week when there was $423 million worth of outflows for \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  products, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-crypto-asset-products-saw-record-weekly-outflows-of-423m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highest amount ever on CoinShares\u8217\'20\'19 records}}}\uc2 . Notably, short BTC funds escaped the carnage that week, posting $15.3 million worth of inflows, while BTC products saw significant outflows of $453 million.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDcvNGI4MDkxNjMtMzA4My00MGUxLTlhM2EtMjRlOWY2YjRiMWI4LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220705ei7500006\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 7/4: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, DOGE, DOT, LEO, SHIB\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,838 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 July 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and select altcoins are indicating that the selling pressure may be reducing in the short term.\par \par \uc2 The crypto markets have remained relatively stable over the weekend and on July 4, which is a holiday for the United States financial markets due to Independence Day. Although Arthur Hayes, former CEO of derivatives platform BitMEX, was expecting a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/wild-ride-lower-for-btc-5-things-to-know-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mega crypto dump\u8221\'20\'1D around July 4}}}\uc2 , it has not materialized.\par \par \uc2 The drop in Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past few days has resulted in the squeezing of the Bollinger Band\u8217\'20\'19s width. This indicates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-addresses-in-loss-hit-all-time-high-amid-18k-btc-price-target"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a possible increase in \b  \highlight22volatility\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in the next few days, according to popular analyst Matthew Hyland.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/875488ce-2e6b-411f-b9b4-7362e7895c84.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, crypto investors seem to be waiting for clues from the U.S. equities markets and the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s correlation coefficient with the dollar in the week ending July 3 slumped to 0.77 below zero, the lowest level in seventeen months. The majority of the analysts surveyed by \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  expect the dollar to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-s-inverse-correlation-with-us-dollar-hits-17-month-highs-what-s-next-for-btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 end at or below the current price levels}}}\uc2  of about 105. Any weakness in the dollar could be beneficial for Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 Could bulls start a recovery in the short term? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bears to extend Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s decline below $19,637 suggests a lack of sellers at lower levels. The bulls will now attempt to push the price back above the resistance at $19,637.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/ced7f131-8139-4d5d-985d-2ef2e00a929c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If that happens, the BTC/USDT pair could rise to the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($21,255). This level could again act as a stiff resistance but if bulls clear this hurdle, the pair may rise to the overhead zone between $22,000 and $23,362.\par \par \uc2 A break above this zone could open the doors for a possible rally to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($25,710). The bulls will have to overcome this barrier to signal a potential trend change.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the sentiment remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  and traders are selling on rallies. That could increase the possibility of a retest of the critical support at $17,622. If this support cracks, the decline could extend to $15,000.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) slipped below the psychological level at $1,000 on June 30 but the bears could not capitalize on this weakness. This suggests that bulls are buying on dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/26886fb8-9e55-4a74-a6a6-31ece40d096d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will now try to push the price above the 20-day EMA ($1,192) and gain the upper hand. If they do that, the ETH/USDT pair could rise to $1,280 and then to the 50-day SMA ($1,535). This level could again act as a strong resistance. The bulls will have to propel the price above $1,700 to signal the start of a new up-move.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the sentiment remains negative and bears are selling on rallies. The bears will then try to sink the price below $998 and challenge the critical support at $881.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 The buyers have successfully defended the support at $211 since June 29, indicating strong demand at lower levels. The bulls are presently attempting to push {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  above the 20-day EMA ($231).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/d8092690-f477-4223-b515-5e4186319405.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, it will suggest that the BNB/USDT pair may have bottomed out at $183. The buyers will then attempt to drive the pair to the 50-day SMA ($266). A break and close above this resistance could signal a potential change in trend.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that bears are selling on every minor rally. The bears will then again try to sink the price below $211 and gain the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  has been trading inside a symmetrical triangle pattern, indicating indecision among the bulls and the bears. The symmetrical triangle usually acts as a continuation pattern but on some occasions, it also behaves as a reversal pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/dddab583-3945-4253-88c5-cef7d8902b81.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price has rebounded off the support line of the triangle and the bulls will attempt to push the XRP/USDT pair above the 20-day EMA ($0.33). If they succeed, the pair could rise to the resistance line of the triangle.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above this level could suggest the start of a new up-move. The pair could then rally to $0.48.\par \par \uc2 Another possibility is that the price turns down sharply from the 20-day EMA and breaks below the support line of the triangle. That could pull the pair down to the critical support at $0.28. If this level cracks, the next stop could be $0.23.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Although Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has been trading near the $0.44 level since June 30, the bears have not been able to pull and sustain the price below the support. This suggests that bulls are buying the dips toward $0.44.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/0fef148f-c353-40eb-9998-c2bc16e896dc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The buyers are currently attempting to push the price above the 20-day EMA ($0.48). If they accomplish this task, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could rise to the 50-day SMA ($0.51). This is an important level to keep an eye on because a break and close above it could suggest that the bears may be losing their grip.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from the moving averages, it will suggest that bears are active at higher levels. The sellers will then try to sink the pair below $0.44 and challenge the critical level at $0.40.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) has been trading just below the 20-day EMA ($35) for the past few days but the bears have not been able to capitalize on this weakness. This suggests a lack of sellers at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/cf142b43-a3e8-4e78-a030-5c452aadca3f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The buyers will now attempt to push the price above the 20-day EMA. If they can pull it off, the SOL/USDT pair could rise to the 50-day SMA ($40). A break and close above this resistance could open the doors for a possible rally to the psychological level at $50.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price turns down from the moving averages, it will suggest that the sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on minor rallies. The bears will then try to pull the pair below $30. If they do that, the pair could decline to $27 and then to $25.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) has been clinging to the 20-day EMA ($0.07) for the past few days. This suggests that the bulls are buying the intraday dips as they expect a move higher.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/2bfcfc2e-2ce5-4489-a8a5-b39a2808b874.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the relative strength index (RSI) is near the midpoint, indicating that the selling pressure may be reducing. The bulls will attempt to push the price above the 50-day SMA ($0.07) and challenge the immediate resistance at $0.08. If this level is crossed, the DOGE/USDT pair could rise to $0.10.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns down from the current level or the 50-day SMA, it will suggest that the bears are defending the moving averages with vigor. The sellers will then try to sink the pair below $0.06 and gain the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/hodlers-and-whales-who-owns-the-most-bitcoin-in-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hodlers and whales: Who owns the most Bitcoin in 2022?}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) has been trading between $7.30 and $6.36 since June 30. This suggests that bulls are buying at lower levels but the bears have not allowed the price to rise above the range.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/26e8367c-56a3-4b14-8800-b7287e561557.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Although the downsloping 20-day EMA ($7.52) indicates advantage to sellers, the positive divergence on the RSI indicates that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could be weakening. If buyers drive the price above the 20-day EMA, the DOT/USDT pair could rally to the 50-day SMA ($8.63).\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view could be invalidated if the price turns down and plummets below the crucial support at $6.36. If that happens, the pair could resume its downtrend toward the next support at $5.\par \par \uc2 LEO/USD\par \par \uc2 The bulls and the bears are battling it out for supremacy near the resistance line of the descending channel. UNUS SED LEO ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/leo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LEO}}}\uc2  ) dipped to the 20-day EMA ($5.65) on July 2 but the bulls successfully defended the level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/ac1a466e-b865-41d2-a462-27c8b704c0bb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LEO/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The buyers are again attempting to clear the resistance line of the channel. The rising 20-day EMA and the RSI in the positive territory indicate that the path of least resistance is to the upside. If the price sustains above $6, the LEO/USD pair {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/what-bear-market-this-token-is-quietly-making-new-highs-up-300-against-bitcoin-in-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could pick up momentum}}}\uc2  and rally to $6.50. Above this level, the rally could extend to the pattern target at $6.90.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price once again turns down from $6, it will suggest that bears are aggressively defending this level. The bears will then attempt to sink the pair below the 20-day EMA. If they manage to do that, the pair could slide to the 50-day SMA ($5.30).\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Shiba Inu ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/shiba-inu-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SHIB}}}\uc2  ) has been trading close to the psychological level at $0.000010. This suggests that the bulls are attempting to form a higher low near this support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/811bdd23-dd06-4f4c-998d-0dca8e150533.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.000010) is flat and the RSI is near the midpoint, indicating a balance between supply and demand. If the price breaks above the 50-day SMA ($0.000010), the SHIB/USDT pair could rally to $0.000012. This level could again act as a stiff barrier but if cleared, the pair could rise to $0.000014.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the moving averages, the bears will try to pull the pair below $0.000009. If they succeed, the pair could retest the critical support at $0.000007.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph.com. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDcvYzkzNjFhODUtYTQ0MC00YTc2LWFmZDAtOGMyMzg2ZDhjYWI0LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220704ei74000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 African celebrities join degens on the journey to the moon\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Elisha Owusu Akyaw \par \uc2 2,378 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 July 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 High costs of living, inflation and a lack of jobs and opportunities have pushed people in Africa toward cryptocurrency adoption\par \par \uc2 African degens are on a journey to the moon. With crypto, African people\u8217\'20\'19s savings are hedged against insane inflation levels, they can find employment in Web3, and there is always the potential to make life-changing money that will transform the trajectory of their lives forever.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/518d3c83-3d98-4cf9-bfe6-93af9b5b80ae.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 People from various backgrounds are embarking on this journey to outer space. These crypto astronauts have, until recently, been hesitant to declare their involvement in the blockchain space. General sentiments around crypto were extremely negative due to the huge slew of scams disguised as cryptocurrency projects that swept through the continent, taking away hard-earned capital and confidence in anything branded with crypto.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not helped in this case either. In most African countries with signs of strong \b \highlight22\uc2 crypto adoption\b0 \highlight\uc2 , central banks issued statements that cast a shadow on the already \u8220\'20\'1Cquestionable\u8221\'20\'1D sector. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cryptocurrency-is-not-legitimate-money-says-nigeria-s-central-bank-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nigeria}}}\uc2 , Ghana, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/zimbabwes-central-bank-bans-financial-institutions-from-all-crypto-dealings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Zimbabwe}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/uganda-bitcoin-queen-bank-of-uganda-warning-only-makes-bitcoin-popular"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uganda}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/central-bank-of-kenya-warns-banks-against-dealing-in-crypto"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kenya}}}\uc2 , regulators took turns issuing warnings to the general public about the dangers involved with crypto. Being involved in crypto would regularly lead to a few chuckles and hostile responses anytime you were bold enough to admit it.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/d426194f-eae7-466e-90c1-1dfaa93b7868.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 A new wind is blowing\par \par \uc2 The situation has changed dramatically in recent times. Real-life examples of early-investors-turned-influencers who acquired property through cryptocurrencies proved to be great ads. Furthermore, the degens who had been given a bad name for so long were relentless about their efforts to share the good news about cryptocurrencies. Those few who dared enter the space despite the bad PR placed a huge emphasis on education, which has resulted in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-users-in-africa-grew-by-2-500-in-2021-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crypto becoming a household name}}}\uc2 . Also, the economic conditions of the last few years made the argument for a decentralized permissionless digital economy more sound than ever.\par \par \uc2 Inside the new class of cryptocurrency adopters is a set of people who truly stand out: celebrities. They are everywhere \u8212\'20\'14 on our screens, on billboards and now in our crypto world. These famous athletes, musicians and actors are joining the space in many ways, but for the sake of this article, I will group them into three groups: promoters, experimenters and the curious.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/here-s-what-s-happening-in-web3-across-africa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s happening in Web3 across Africa}}}\par \par \uc2 Promoters\par \par \uc2 As established already, the negative PR that crypto has faced in Africa means that lots of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/in-defense-of-crypto-why-digital-currencies-deserve-a-better-reputation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rebranding and promotion}}}\uc2  are needed. The huge interest in crypto on the continent has attracted some big spenders, such as Binance and FTX, which have large marketing budgets. Homegrown companies like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/african-crypto-exchange-registers-3-2b-in-transactions-ahead-of-global-expansion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Quidax}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/african-crypto-exchange-yellow-card-closes-15m-series-a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yellow Card}}}\uc2 , which want to keep up with these international companies, have also adopted similar spending habits. A major feature of the marketing plans of all three companies mentioned is the inclusion of celebrities.\par \par \uc2 Binance is spending big in Africa. In early 2022 alone, Binance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-sponsors-afcon-to-further-develop-crypto-adoption-in-africa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sponsored the African Cup of Nations}}}\uc2  in Cameroon and Nigerian Idol. Including popular faces in its education drive is a core part of its marketing efforts. In December 2021, the exchange signed deals with reality TV show Big Brother Naija participants Hazel Oyeze Onou, popularly known as Whitemoney; Ikechukwu Sunday Okonkwo, known as Cross; and Pere Egbi, known simply as Pere. Since the announcement, the trio has been featured in several educational videos targeted at potential new users of cryptocurrency.\par \par \uc2 FTX is also making huge marketing moves on the continent. In an attempt to attract a female demographic, which has been hard to reach, FTX Africa partnered with six female celebrities to push Web3, including actor Cynthia Nwadiora, actor Beverly Naya, lifestyle influencer Aunty \b \highlight22\uc2 Ada\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Big Brother Naija star Saskay, TV personality Serwaa Amihere and actor Osas Ighodaro.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/women-s-interest-in-crypto-grows-but-education-gap-persists-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s interest in crypto grows, but education gap persists}}}\par \par \uc2 Nigeria-based Quidax is not slowing down as it intends to compete with various international exchanges entering the market. In March 2022, the exchange announced popular Nigerian music producer Don Jazzy as its brand ambassador alongside five other celebrities: Diane Russet and Bisola Aiyeola \u8212\'20\'14 both actors and reality TV stars \u8212\'20\'14 actor Timini Egbuson, celebrity chef Gbubemi Fregene and musician M.I Abaga.\par \par \uc2 Yellow Card is another exchange based in Nigeria looking to capture market share on the continent. The exchange announced a partnership with Ghanaian dancehall artist Stonebwoy to spread crypto awareness in West Africa.\par \par \uc2 Experimenters\par \par \uc2 Another set of celebrities who have entered the space are the experimenters. These big names have set the stage for blockchain technology to be used to amplify creativity and harness new ways to connect with fandoms through nonfungible tokens (NFTs), the Metaverse and fan tokens.\par \par \uc2 In Nigeria, Bnxn and Falz are two of the biggest artists to have released an NFT. Bnxn (formerly known as Buju) launched HeadsByBnxn, a collection of 10,001 NFTs designed around him and his journey in the music industry. The project was launched on the Polygon blockchain to make minting more affordable. Holders are treated to exclusive listening parties and in-person and virtual shows.\par \par \uc2 Falz, another popular artist, landed a deal with the Binance NFT Marketplace, where he exclusively sells his Falz Ice Cream collection. Like Bnxn\u8217\'20\'19s collection, there are exclusive experiences for people holding the NFTs. I had the chance to speak to Falz about his collection on Cointelegraph\u8217\'20\'19s flagship Twitter Spaces show, Crypto Talk Africa. As he said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith this [NFTs], I think it not only offers a different avenue for artists to exploit their intellectual property, it also offers an avenue to organically build a community, you know? And this latter one is what I\u8217\'20\'19m very excited about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Why are musicians jumping on the NFT hype? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/falzthebahdguy?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @falzthebahdguy}}}\uc2  is excited about the ability to build a community organically using nonfungible tokens.\par \par \uc2 What is your favorite NFT by a celeb? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IuQOlfUr9O"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IuQOlfUr9O}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Cointelegraph (@Cointelegraph) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Cointelegraph/status/1524091146518994944?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 KiDi, the reigning Ghana Music Awards artist of the year, is a recent addition to the long list of celebrities releasing NFTs. His two-tier drop is set to come with multiple utilities. In a \uc2 YouTube\uc2  video about the drop, KiDi claims that the lower tier, KiDi Classic, will give global fans a sense of ownership of his craft. The higher tier, KiDi VIP Pass, will reward fans with discounts at physical and virtual events and exclusive virtual parties.\par \par \uc2 In Kenya, hip-hop star Octopizzo announced that he would be releasing five songs as nonfungible tokens. His approach is very different from the rest, as he is set to release fractional NFTs that will give holders a share of royalties.\par \par \uc2 Kenyan hip hop star, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/OCTOPIZZO?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @octopizzo}}}\uc2 , will be releasing 5 tracks as NFTs that can be purchased by anyone in Africa and the world on OpenSea. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/mynftafrica?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #mynftafrica}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/nftafrica?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #nftafrica}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/nft?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #nft}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/kenya?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #kenya}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/nfts?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #nfts}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/nftcollection?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #nftcollection}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/nftgiveaway?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #nftgiveaway}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GCx90Xpaso"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GCx90Xpaso}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NFT AFRICA (@myNFTAfrica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/myNFTAfrica/status/1495409341406617604?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Kwaito musician DJ Sbu became one of the first artists in South Africa to release an NFT. The \u8220\'20\'1CDJ Sbu Enters The Metaverse\u8221\'20\'1D collection sold 10 pieces in three days. The DJ has since indicated plans to release other collections in the future after the success of the first.\par \par \uc2 Not everyone is experimenting with NFTs, however. Unlike other people mentioned in this section, popular Afrobeats and Afropop artist Davido (whose real name is David Adedeji Adeleke) opted to launch a fan token.\par \par \uc2 The ECHOKE token was announced in November 2021. It is expected to run on BNB Smart Chain and offer holders the ability to attend festivals, buy merchandise, get concert tickets and enter exclusive giveaways.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s still too early to issue a verdict on how successful these experiments have been; however, the level of activity by creatives in the space points to a lot of potential for the adoption of blockchain technology in the entertainment sector.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/celebrities-are-embracing-nfts-in-a-big-way"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Celebrities are embracing NFTs in a big way}}}\par \par \uc2 The curious\par \par \uc2 Probably the group closest to the word \u8220\'20\'1Cdegen,\u8221\'20\'1D the curious celebrities are not just promoting cryptocurrencies but are knee-deep in the space and are known to be power users.\par \par \uc2 One such celebrity is Don Jazzy, a music producer behind hit songs from major names like Ayra Starr and Rema. In an interview with Chris Ani on Daba TV, Don Jazzy revealed that he made $300,000 in a short period from NFT sales. In an \uc2 Instagram\uc2  post showing his NFT collection, some blue-chip NFTs such as Cool Cats and Mutant Ape Yacht Club were spotted. Don Jazzy has also become a regular fixture on Crypto \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , offering support for some African NFT projects, such as AfroDroids.\par \par \uc2 Symply Tacha is another celebrity active in the cryptocurrency community. Tacha has become a household name on African Crypto \uc2 Twitter\uc2  for her NFT investments and community engagements. She is so popular that new NFT projects partner with her for whitelist giveaways and promotions.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s hard to tell how many celebrities really fall under this category, as some may prefer to keep their investments private.\par \par \uc2 A welcome addition or not?\par \par \uc2 Opinions are split on the increase of celebrity participation in the crypto space. One side of the debate believes that celebrities are a welcome addition, while the other side believes that all of this is just a quick cash grab.\par \par \uc2 The biggest opposition thus far came after the launch of FTX Africa\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CWomen Who Crypto\u8221\'20\'1D campaign, which involved partnering with several female celebrities to promote crypto in an attempt to attract women to the space. Crypto \uc2 Twitter\uc2  quickly erupted with several critics of the initiative. The overarching argument was that the campaign could have relied on women already in the crypto space instead of celebrities who may not be as blockchain-native.\par \par \uc2 Some of these comments came from influencers such as UnkleAyo and Ademi.\par \par \uc2 To say the least, this is a disrespect to women who actually grind in the space!\par \par \uc2 Not one of them on? And you want to onboard into web3?\par \par \uc2 Top off my head active traders and builders in this space and NONE of this women will land top 50.\par \par \uc2 BBN Web3? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Z8UOeqIvfa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Z8UOeqIvfa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \u176\'00\'B0S.A.L.A.K.O\u8482\'21\'22 (@UnkleAyo) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UnkleAyo/status/1512055629518671880?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Shame on FTX though.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m a woman in Crypto from Africa and none of the women in Crypto making Impact are even here. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/g2CBZ2QvM3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/g2CBZ2QvM3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ademi (@Ademiici) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Ademiici/status/1512056932076511234?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 I asked Harri Obi, marketing and public relations lead at FTX Africa, about the rationale behind the campaign and his reaction to the ad\u8217\'20\'19s feedback. This was his answer:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo be honest, we anticipated the response. Conversations around women in the Web3 space, or lack thereof, have always elicited heavy arguments from supporters and non-supporters alike. And that was really our goal \u8212\'20\'14 to spark up a conversation around the subject matter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harri continued: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you followed the conversation that day, there was a mixed reaction to the ad. People were confused about the lack of crypto representation in the ad, but when we explained the idea behind the ad and the goal, the sentiments started changing. But most importantly, we\u8217\'20\'19ve gone on to develop and execute tactical executions of the campaign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Osaretin Victor Asemota, a crypto pioneer and retired investor, believes that crypto needs to put on a serious face and position its power users at the forefront instead of attention-grabbing celebrities:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need people to take crypto seriously and have to find serious users to endorse crypto. I don\u8217\'20\'19t like the celebrity endorsements, even though I have nothing against the celebrities. It is just grabbing for attention and using models similar to those that seemed to work elsewhere. We have different types of celebrities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asemota continued: \u8220\'20\'1CThey live in a world far removed from our reality. I think the real celebrity we need to promote crypto is the African trader. They made crypto scale, and their stories need to be told. They are the people who need it, and we need more like them. Crypto in Africa is more of an infrastructure for commerce than investing in assets.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-firms-ignore-africa-at-their-peril-as-continent-set-for-major-adoption"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto firms ignore Africa at their peril as continent set for major adoption}}}\par \par \uc2 The crypto future for Africa\par \par \uc2 At the end of the day, everyone has a role to play in ensuring that crypto gets the recognition and adoption we want. The promoters, experimenters and curious are all bringing people to cryptocurrencies. Promoters directly point users to specific apps and products, which is extremely important considering the overwhelming nature of the space for newbies. Experimenters bring a crowd of users who would traditionally not look twice at crypto. For example, someone may not be interested in buying \u8220\'20\'1Cbeautiful art\u8221\'20\'1D NFTs but could be attracted to digital collectibles because that is the only way to connect to their favorite artist on a personal level. Finally, the curious could be a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  case for people looking for examples around them of those who have made money from the crypto space or some sort of significant investment.\par \par \uc2 These celebrities have built huge followings, which is extremely important for the mainstream recognition that cryptocurrency wants. However, some critics point to important issues that we have to look into. Celebrities may have to put more skin in the game to prevent pump and dumps and the promotion of questionable projects for a quick paycheck. With a troubling brand image that only got cleaner recently, perhaps brands, celebrities, and stakeholders have to tread cautiously to prevent further controversy that may derail all the work done in the last few years.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 The views, thoughts and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par \uc2 Elisha Owusu Akyaw, also known as GhCryptoGuy, is a social media specialist at Cointelegraph. He got involved in cryptocurrencies at 16 and took it upon himself to educate the masses about crypto. Elisha has worked as a freelance writer for several blogs and is a former business developer for Binance in Ghana.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDYvNDc5MTcwYWItYTJiZC00OTQzLWJhZGEtNDQ0NzJmOGE1ZmRjLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220702ei720002u\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin will see \u8216\'20\'18long bear market\u8217\'20\'19 says trader with BTC price stuck at $19K\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  William Suberg \par \uc2 616 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 July 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 BTC price action is tipped to continue downhill with Bitcoin traders predicting an enduring bear market.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) failed to reclaim recent losses into July 2 as traders prepared for stagnant price action to continue.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/cbb989a5-cfcc-41d5-a25c-f552f1dbc3d1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 1-hour candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 "Downtrend acceleration" still in force\par \par \uc2 Data from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.cointelegraph.com/?via=markets&_ga=2.142027444.742658523.1640948929-762064149.1640948929"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph Markets Pro}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSD/?exchange=BINANCE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\uc2  tracked a limp BTC/USD as it chopped around the $19,000 mark into the weekend.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street trading week had finished without surprises, with United States equities practically stagnant \u8212\'20\'14 providing little impetus for crypto \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The U.S. dollar index, or DXY, fresh from a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-nears-worst-monthly-losses-since-2011-with-btc-price-at-19k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retest}}}\uc2  of twenty-year highs, ran out of steam to circle 105 points.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/978b1a8f-b935-47e3-a526-f483b0ac078e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 U.S. dollar index (DXY) 1-hour candle chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Order book data from largest global exchange \uc2 Binance\uc2  showed BTC/USD caught between buy and sell liquidity close to spot price, ensuring a lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  until traders maneuvered or added significantly to bids or asks.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/d43d6747-539b-4455-a621-b890613c8fda.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD order book data (Binance). Source: Material Indicators\par \par \uc2 Zooming out, the outlook hardly seemed any more optimistic for bulls.\par \par \uc2 For popular trading account Altcoin Sherpa, current conditions promised an extended period of uninspiring performance from Bitcoin which could last much of 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIts gonna take months to chop around and accumulate once the bottom is found,\u8221\'20\'1D it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AltcoinSherpa/status/1542931992404234241"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2 Twitter\uc2  followers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the bottom might not even come for another few months from today. Hunker down for a long bear market IMO.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The sentiment was echoed by trader and analyst Rekt Capital, who argued that Bitcoin had not yet made new macro lows or started to consolidate.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BTC?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BTC}}}\uc2  may still very well be in the \u8220\'20\'1CDowntrend Acceleration\u8221\'20\'1D phase of its correction\par \par \uc2 But this phase will precede the \u8220\'20\'1CMulti-Month Consolidation\u8221\'20\'1D phase\par \par \uc2 Which will precede the \u8220\'20\'1CNew Macro Uptrend\u8221\'20\'1D phase {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BTC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Crypto?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Crypto}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Bitcoin?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Bitcoin}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rekt Capital (@rektcapital) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rektcapital/status/1542902502152093697?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 1, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDeleverage yourself. Get your Bitcoin into cold storage. Sit tight,\u8221\'20\'1D Checkmate, lead on-chain analyst at research firm Glassnode {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/_Checkmatey_/status/1542993068739133440"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Will volume all-time highs echo 2018?\par \par \uc2 The next week or two could prove to be this cycle's lows, meanwhile, lending a degree of hope to those concerned that the bottom is still months away.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/price-analysis-7-1-btc-eth-bnb-xrp-ada-sol-doge-dot-leo-shib"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 7/1: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , SOL, DOGE, DOT, LEO, SHIB}}}\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/krugermacro/status/1543136013794414592"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter thread}}}\uc2  on the day, economist, trader and entrepreneur Alex Krueger noted that volume denominated in BTC hit all-time highs last month.\par \par \uc2 "As a general rule, trading volume is the highest when markets capitulate," he explained.\par \par \uc2 As a general rule, trading volume is the highest when markets capitulate, and such capitulation creates major bottoms.\par \par \uc2 This weekly chart includes the aggregated bitcoin volume for most BTC pairs (spot & perpetuals across exchanges).\par \par \uc2 Volume hit its all time high two weeks ago. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6ONLibQiL2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6ONLibQiL2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alex Kr\u252\'00\'FCger (@krugermacro) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/krugermacro/status/1543136013794414592?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 In the 2018 bear market, he added, the volume all-time high in fact occurred several weeks before the price bottom, and should this time follow the trend, July could be the site of the next.\par \par \uc2 Previously, Rekt Capital had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-crashes-to-20-8k-as-deadly-candles-liquidate-1-2-billion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  that buy-side volume had not been strong enough to sustain fresh price upside in the long term, while also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-clings-to-20k-as-analysts-warn-of-a-long-bumpy-ride-for-the-foreseeable-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highlighting}}}\uc2  the 2018 volume moves.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph.com. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDcvMDFmNDBkY2YtNDYzZC00ZmI1LWIwOTItNzkyMjRkZmZhYmFkLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220702ei720002t\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 7/1: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, DOGE, DOT, LEO, SHIB\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,827 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 July 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Traders expect Bitcoin to swoop below its swing low before the price flattens out and altcoins begin to recover.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin dropped 56.2% in the second quarter of 2022, according to crypto analytics platform Coinglass. That makes it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/worst-quarter-in-11-years-as-bitcoin-price-and-activity-plunges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s worst quarter}}}\uc2  since the third quarter of 2011 when BTC price fell by 67%. A large part of the damage was done in the month of June when Bitcoin plunged 37%, the worst monthly drawdown since September 2011.\par \par \uc2 It is not all gloom and doom for crypto investors. On June 29, \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  strategist \uc2 Nikolaos Panigirtzoglou\uc2  said that the \u8220\'20\'1CNet Leverage metric\u8221\'20\'1D suggests that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/better-days-ahead-with-crypto-deleveraging-coming-to-an-end-jpmorgan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crypto\u8217\'20\'19s deleveraging may be on its last legs}}}\uc2 . The eagerness of crypto companies with stronger balance sheets to bail out crypto firms in distress is also a positive sign.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/94f52aae-815c-4154-bedf-797f6db2b7da.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Another positive view on Bitcoin came from \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  analysts. In a recent report, the strategists said that the S&P 500 could recover lost ground and rally to the levels seen in January. This could benefit Bitcoin due to its close correlation with the S&P 500.\par \par \uc2 Could the downtrend resume or will lower levels attract buyers? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin plummeted below the immediate support at $19,637 on June 30 but the long tail on the candlestick indicates strong buying at lower levels. The bulls tried to build upon the momentum on July 1 and push the price toward the overhead resistance at $22,000 but the long wick on the candlestick shows that bears are active at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/168610b4-3ece-4698-a19b-dade7d5fba1d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains below $19,637, the likelihood of a retest of the critical support at $17,622 increases. The downsloping moving averages and the relative strength index in the oversold zone indicate that bears are in control.\par \par \uc2 A break and close below $17,622 could signal the resumption of the downtrend. The next support is at $15,000.\par \par \uc2 This negative view could invalidate in the short term if the price rises above the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($21,907). Such a move could clear the path for a possible rally to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($26,361).\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) dipped below the immediate support of $1,050 on June 30 but the bulls purchased the dip. The buyers tried to extend the recovery on July 1 but the long wick on the candlestick shows that bears are selling on minor rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/9e5d02be-3dce-4225-953a-40273bd3cf4c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will try to pull the price below the psychological level of $1,000. If they succeed, the selling could pick up momentum and the ETH/USDT pair could drop to the important support at $881. If this level gives way, the pair could resume the downtrend. The next support is at $681.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price rebounds off the current level or $1,000, the bulls will attempt to push the pair above the 20-day EMA. If they can pull it off, it will suggest that bears may be losing their grip. The \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could pick up on a break above $1,280.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  dipped below the strong support at $211 on June 30 but the lower levels attracted strong buying as seen from the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/1d86d34e-dec3-4c86-90ed-bf5c27542f07.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The buyers tried to extend the recovery on July 1 but the long wick on the candlestick shows that bears are defending the 20-day EMA ($234) aggressively. The downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the negative territory indicate advantage to sellers.\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains below $211, the BNB/USDT pair could retest the crucial support at $183. If this support cracks, the downtrend could resume. The next support is at $150.\par \par \uc2 This negative view could invalidate in the short term if the price turns up and breaks above the 20-day EMA. That could clear the path for a possible rally to the 50-day SMA ($271).\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) attempted a recovery on June 30 but the bulls could not push the price above the overhead resistance at $0.35. This suggests that bears are not willing to let go of their advantage.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/d0446f45-a2f4-4f9f-bd11-beb70bd8676a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The XRP/USDT pair could drop to the strong support at $0.28 where the bulls are likely to mount a strong defense. If the price rebounds off $0.28, it will suggest that bulls continue to buy at lower levels. The bulls will then make one more attempt to push the price above the 50-day SMA ($0.37).\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if bears sink the price below $0.28, the next leg of the downtrend could begin. The pair could then decline to $0.23.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) bounced off $0.44 on June 30 but the bulls could not clear the 20-day EMA ($0.49) on July 1. This suggests that bears continue to defend the moving averages with vigor.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/8e0c3ce6-4506-438e-8a29-fbf51bead4c2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the negative zone indicate that the path of least resistance is to the downside. If the price slips below $0.44, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could drop to the critical support of $0.40.\par \par \uc2 The bulls are expected to defend this level with all their might because if the support cracks, the pair could resume its downtrend. The next support is at $0.33.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price rebounds off $0.44 or $0.40, the buyers will again try to clear the overhead resistance at the moving averages. If they succeed, the pair could start a relief rally toward $0.70.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) dipped below the immediate support at $33 on June 30 but the long tail on the candlestick shows strong buying at lower levels. The buyers tried to push the price above the 20-day EMA ($36) on July 1 but the bears did not relent.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/7d732793-bb13-4bbc-830b-1fe3c0cb5fba.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The sellers will try to gain the upper hand by pulling the price below $30. If they manage to do that, the SOL/USDT pair could drop to $27 and later to the crucial support at $25.86. A break and close below this level could signal the resumption of the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 Another possibility is that the price rebounds off $30. That will indicate accumulation at lower levels. The bulls will then try to clear the overhead hurdle at the moving averages and push the price to $50.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) is witnessing a tough battle between the bulls and the bears near the 20-day EMA ($0.07). The RSI is just below the midpoint and the 20-day EMA has flattened out, indicating a minor advantage to sellers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/84f86a9c-b6ce-4ad9-83c4-ed924bad77af.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price slips below $0.06, it will suggest that bears are back in the driver\u8217\'20\'19s seat. The sellers will then attempt to sink the DOGE/USDT pair below the important support at $0.05 and resume the downtrend. The next support is at $0.04.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price rises from the current level, the buyers will again attempt to clear the overhead hurdle at the 50-day SMA ($0.08). If they succeed, it will suggest that the bears may be losing their grip. The pair could then rally to the strong overhead resistance at $0.10.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/what-bear-market-this-token-is-quietly-making-new-highs-up-300-against-bitcoin-in-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What bear market? This token is quietly making new highs, up 300% against Bitcoin in 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) broke and closed below the strong support at $7.30 on June 29. The buyers tried to push the price back above the level on June 30 but failed. This suggests that bears are selling on every minor rally.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/71fae71d-1333-461b-83ef-da31def86489.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($7.74) has started to turn down and the RSI is in the negative territory, indicating that bears are in command. If the price breaks below $6.36, the DOT/USDT pair could start the next leg of the downtrend. The next support is at $5.00.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price rebounds off the current level, the bulls will again attempt to clear the overhead resistance at the 20-day EMA. If they succeed, the pair could rally to the 50-day SMA ($8.89).\par \par \uc2 LEO/USD\par \par \uc2 UNUS SED LEO ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/leo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LEO}}}\uc2  ) turned down on June 30 but the bulls did not allow the price to slip back into the descending channel. This indicates that buyers are trying to flip the resistance line into support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/3198b845-ee7f-4b72-8b0f-333d4b81e84a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LEO/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The breakout from the channel indicates the start of a new up-move. The buyers pushed the price to $6.50 on July 1 but the long wick on the candlestick shows that bears are selling on rallies. If bulls sustain the price above $6.00, the LEO/USD pair may again rise to $6.50. If this level is cleared, the rally could extend to the pattern target of $6.90.\par \par \uc2 To invalidate this \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view, the bears will have to pull the price below the 20-day EMA ($5.63). If that happens, the pair may drop to the 50-day SMA ($5.27).\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Shiba Inu ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/shiba-inu-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SHIB}}}\uc2  ) closed below $0.000010 on June 28 but the bears could sustain the lower levels. The bulls bought the dip but are struggling to push the price above the 50-day SMA ($0.000010)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/6beaf249-054f-4dcb-8928-fa157bbad8ef.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages have flattened out and the RSI is just below the midpoint. This suggests a status of equilibrium between the buyers and sellers. If the price breaks below $0.000009, it will suggest an advantage to bears. The SHIB/USDT pair could then decline to the crucial support of $0.000007.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if bulls drive the price above the 50-day SMA, the pair could rise to $0.000012. This level may again act as a resistance but if crossed, the rally may reach $0.000014.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDcvNTRmNWI1NGYtMWNlZS00YTNkLWJlZWUtOGNhNDhlNjNhN2E5LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220701ei71000e3\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 June gloom takes on a new meaning in another 2022 down month\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Cointelegraph Consulting \par \uc2 964 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 July 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin dropped another 33% in June, which is now beginning to numb the \uc2 Twitter\uc2  community.\par \par \uc2 The market cap of Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) dropped another 33% in June, which is now beginning to numb the \uc2 Twitter\uc2  community. On the upside, many crypto traders who wanted out did so fairly aggressively from March to May. But, the less optimistic news is that the stagnancy in address activity may need to change for prices to get a running start on recovery.\par \par \uc2 Unlike April and May, the altcoin pack didn\u8217\'20\'19t struggle tremendously more than Bitcoin. BTC\u8217\'20\'19s 33% drop was pretty middle of the road in terms of corrections. In a vacuum, crypto bulls would prefer seeing altcoins continuing to lag, pushing more traders back toward Bitcoin as a relative \u8220\'20\'1Csafe haven.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, June was a tale of two halves. June 1-15 saw a massive 25% further downswing for Bitcoin. Comparatively, June 16-30 was looking up until the very end of the month, which now exhibits an additional 8% slide.\par \par \uc2 The $20,000 price level has shown to be both psychological support and resistance area. Therefore, a drop below (which could very well occur by the time this article is published) may quickly change traders\u8217\'20\'19 outlook. Panic selling and overly eager buying should occur as soon as the $19,500 to $19,900 range is hit.\par \par \uc2 Social dominance has returned to Bitcoin and away from altcoins\par \par \uc2 So far, 2022 has served as a reality check for altcoins whose market caps have ballooned to astronomic levels in the past two years. As mentioned, Bitcoin was nothing special compared to alts in June, but it has held up better than most projects and even a few stablecoins. As a result, the spotlight shines bright on Bitcoin, as evidenced by a healthy community focus.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/373ffc2e-c564-4697-8aaa-c51542838c56.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 This phenomenon was reflected in the whole last week of June. Bitcoin was mentioned on Santiment\u8217\'20\'19s social platforms at its highest rate in about four months, while the discussion around other popular assets like Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) and Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) continues to diminish.\par \par \uc2 Trading returns still point to a major undervaluation of Bitcoin and most altcoins\par \par \uc2 The average 30-day trading returns on the BTC network are still very negative. And, as long they are in the yellow-green or green territory in the below chart, there is less risk in entering a Bitcoin position (or adding on to) than historical results.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/814fe280-6e6a-4d75-8620-572a56164616.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Price freefalls tend to reverse if they go into the extreme low (green) territory, and that would be the ideal setup to watch for on Sanbase.\par \par \uc2 The number of whale addresses is growing rapidly\par \par \uc2 Another positive note for patient crypto hodlers, regardless of the asset, is that more and more Bitcoin shark and whale addresses are returning to the network. The addresses, mainly run by active human traders, sized 10 to 10,000 BTC, have over 147,000 addresses for the first time since November. Meanwhile, the very top-tier addresses owned primarily by exchanges (10,000 or more) showed over 100 addresses for the first time since December 2020.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/dcdaf792-ecca-4819-8c08-5fc0c0445097.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 And, speaking of supply moving on and off-exchange addresses, the overall trend shows BTC continuing to move away from exchanges after a brief worrisome rise in May. Now, well below 10% of coins sitting on exchanges, there is far less selloff risk (based on historical trends). And, to add to this, the amount of Tether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tether-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDT}}}\uc2  ) moving to exchanges has skyrocketed, implying more buying power at these suppressed prices.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/4e17298d-2045-4a63-9bc3-d1828ab85097.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Ethereum seeing far more negativity than any other large-cap asset\par \par \uc2 Not to be ignored, Ethereum has had a well-documented 76% retracement since its all-time high in November. When looking at the ratio of positive vs. negative commentary being scraped by our social data algorithm, there appears to be a stunning dropoff in positive comments in early June. The 37% \b \highlight22\uc2 price drop\b0 \highlight\uc2  between June 9 and 13 was the culprit and the last straw for many traders. As counterintuitive as it may seem, these \u8220\'20\'1Clast straws\u8221\'20\'1D is what the community at Santiment expects to see for the market to stage a comeback.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-07/53a4bc4f-d080-42cb-a5b3-0dd712307036.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Cardano is also seeing the equivalent of slowly rolling tumbleweeds around its network. The number of unique addresses interacting on the Cardano network is down to its lowest in about a year. The sentiment is gradually sinking for Cardano as well, which is likely due to a simple absence of discussion more than anything.\par \par \uc2 Traders heading into the second half with extreme skepticism\par \par \uc2 It is hard for the trading community to find any excitement in the abysmal price performances that continue to persist month after month in 2022. Yet, price surges happen when the mainstream casts the most doubts. Still, nothing is for certain in a sentiment-driven and often self-perpetuating sector like cryptocurrency. But, the more the crypto community is leaning \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  and proclaiming its crypto winter time, the higher the chance of a recovery underway.\par \par \uc2 Cointelegraph\u8217\'20\'19s Market Insights Newsletter shares our knowledge on the fundamentals that move the \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. This analysis was prepared by leading analytics provider Santiment, a market intelligence platform that provides on-chain, social media and development information on 2,000+ cryptocurrencies.\par \par \uc2 Santiment develops hundreds of tools, strategies and indicators to help users better understand cryptocurrency market behavior and identify data-driven investment opportunities.\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: The opinions expressed in the post are for general informational purposes only and are not intended to provide specific advice or recommendations for any individual or on any specific security or investment product.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDcvMGRhMjExYWQtZTZiYi00YTU1LTgzZTctMWM3MGI5ODNlYTJmLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220701ei71000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 6/29: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, DOGE, DOT, SHIB, LEO\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,781 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and altcoins gave up the gains of last week\u8217\'20\'19s relief rally and today\u8217\'20\'19s dip below $20,000 suggests bears are intent on pushing the market back to its yearly lows.\par \par \uc2 The United States equities markets have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-limps-under-20k-as-asia-extends-global-stocks-weakness"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 given back some of the gains}}}\uc2  made last week and that has pulled Bitcoin to the psychological support at $20,000. This suggests that investors are nervous to buy risky assets at higher levels.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, while speaking to the hosts of the Bankless podcast on June 23, Mark Cuban said that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bear-market-will-last-until-crypto-apps-are-actually-useful-mark-cuban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crypto bear market could end}}}\uc2  after the price gets so cheap that investors go and start buying or an application with utility is launched that attracts users.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/08c097ce-b759-489f-808d-508608811839.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Several analysts expect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/key-bitcoin-price-metrics-say-btc-bottomed-but-traders-still-fear-a-drop-to-10k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin to continue falling}}}\uc2  and eventually bottom out between $10,000 and $12,000. However, \uc2 John Bollinger\uc2 , the creator of the popular {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/trading-for-beginners/crypto-charts-101-how-to-read-cryptocurrency-charts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bollinger Bands trading indicator}}}\uc2 , said that the monthly charts suggest that Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s price has reached \u8220\'20\'1Ca logical place to put in a bottom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Could bears maintain the selling pressure and pull cryptocurrency prices lower? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin turned down from $22,000 on June 26 and has gradually slipped to the immediate support at $19,637. This suggests that the bears remain in command and every rally is being sold into.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/d26a5f10-2da0-4643-9d79-4fda6fb2d787.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price breaks below $19,637, the BTC/USDT pair could be at risk of dropping to the crucial support at $17,622. This is an important level to watch out for because a break and close below it could start the next leg of the downtrend. The pair could then decline to $15,000.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price rebounds off $19,637, it will suggest demand at lower levels. The buyers will then try to push the price above the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($22,393). If they succeed, the pair could rally to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($26,735).\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 20-day EMA ($1,268) on June 26 suggesting that the sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/ecbe77ef-742e-4d70-9878-aeda1adb272e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping moving averages and the RSI in the negative zone indicate that bears are in control. The sellers will attempt to pull the price below the immediate support at $1,050. If they succeed, the ETH/USDT pair could plunge to the June 18 intraday low of $881.\par \par \uc2 A break below this support could signal the resumption of the downtrend. The next support on the downside is at $681.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price rebounds off $1,050, it will suggest demand at lower levels. The buyers will then make another attempt to push the price above the 20-day EMA and start the journey toward $1,500 and later $1,700.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 The buyers failed to push and sustain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  above the 20-day EMA ($238) between June 24 to 28. This resulted in profit-booking, which has pulled the price to the strong support of $211.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/03852c9e-1e23-4a8d-99bd-ea620583346b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to turn down once again and the RSI has dipped into the negative territory. This suggests that bears have the upper hand. If the price slides below $211, the BNB/USDT pair could drop to the critical support of $183. If this support collapses, the pair could resume its downtrend and plummet toward $150.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rebounds off $211, it will suggest that bulls are attempting to form a higher low. A strong bounce could increase the prospects of a break above $250. The pair could then rally to the 50-day SMA ($273).\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) slipped below the breakout level of $0.35 on June 28 which suggests that bears continue to sell aggressively at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/33a30675-daa1-4cb4-91d1-eb27708feacc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.35) is flattish but the RSI has dropped below 40, suggesting that the bears have a slight edge. The sellers will attempt to pull the price to the vital support at $0.28. This is an important level to keep an eye on because if it gives way, the XRP/USDT pair could start the next leg of the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns up from the current level or $0.28, it will suggest that bulls are buying at lower levels. That could keep the pair range-bound between $0.28 and the 50-day SMA ($0.38) for a few days.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 The bears thwarted repeated attempts by the bulls to push Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($0.50) in the past few days. This suggests that the bears are defending the level aggressively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/a0835baf-5d8a-43a2-9108-4abd16ce399b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price could drop to the strong support zone at $0.44 to $0.40. If the price rebounds off this zone with strength, it will suggest that bulls are accumulating on dips. The buyers will then again try to propel the price above the moving averages. If they can pull it off, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could start an up-move toward $0.70.\par \par \uc2 This positive view could invalidate in the short term if bears sink the pair below the support zone. If that happens, the pair could indicate the resumption of the downtrend. The next support is at $0.33.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 The tight range trading in Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) resolved to the downside with a break below the 20-day EMA ($37). The bears are attempting to pull the price below the immediate support at $33.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/44f1db58-3297-44a4-afc2-4b576a8b8c7c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the SOL/USDT pair could decline to $27 and then retest the June 14 intraday low of $25.86.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price rebounds off $33, it will suggest that the bulls are attempting to form a higher low. The buyers will then try to clear the overhead hurdle at $43. If that happens, the pair could signal a potential change in trend. The pair may then rise to $60 where the bears may again mount a strong defense.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 50-day SMA ($0.08) on June 27 and broke below the 20-day EMA ($0.07) on June 28. This suggests that bears have not given up and they continue to sell on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/655c5a78-a487-4105-9cc4-58f5916366b1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will try to sink the price to $0.06. If this level cracks, the next stop could be a retest of the critical level at $0.05.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns up from the current level or the support at $0.06 and rises back above the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that bulls are attempting to form a higher low. The \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could pick up on a break above $0.08. The DOGE/USDT pair could then attempt a rally to the psychological level of $0.10.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/double-bubble-terra-s-defunct-unstablecoin-suddenly-climbs-800-in-one-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Double bubble? Terra's defunct 'unstablecoin' suddenly climbs 800% in one week}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Repeated failures to push and sustain the price above the 20-day EMA ($7.93) may have tempted short-term traders to book profits in Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ). The price turned down from the 20-day EMA and slipped to $7.30 on June 28.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/ebbc75dd-7bfc-4bf7-b5e3-b6c47abc9ace.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Both the bulls and the bears are battling it out for supremacy near the $7.30 level. If the bears come out on top, the DOT/USDT pair could drop to the crucial level of $6.36. The bulls are expected to defend this level aggressively because a break below it could signal the resumption of the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rebounds off the current level, the buyers will again try to achieve a close above the 20-day EMA. If they manage to do that, the pair could rise to the 50-day SMA ($8.97).\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Shiba Inu ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/shiba-inu-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SHIB}}}\uc2  ) slipped back below the 50-day SMA ($0.000011) on June 28, suggesting that the bears are active at higher levels. Although the price dipped below $0.000010, the bears have not been able to build upon this advantage.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/556b7f55-9bf4-444b-9fbf-c37287526b5c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This suggests that selling dries up at lower levels. The bulls will again try to push the price above the 50-day SMA and challenge the resistance at $0.000012. A break and close above this level could open the doors for a possible rally to $0.000014.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.000010) has flattened out and the RSI is just below the midpoint, indicating a balance between supply and demand. If the price slips below $0.000009, the advantage could tilt in favor of the sellers. The pair may then drop to $0.000007.\par \par \uc2 LEO/USD\par \par \uc2 UNUS SED LEO ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/leo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LEO}}}\uc2  ) broke and closed above the resistance line of the descending channel on June 25 but the bulls could not push the price above $6. That may have attracted profit-booking from short-term traders, which pulled the price back into the channel on June 27.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/4f59fd1a-c1e4-471e-9ed5-42bd58b569d0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LEO/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($5.57) is sloping up and the RSI is in the positive territory suggesting that bulls have the upper hand. The buyers are again attempting to clear the overhead hurdle at $6. If they succeed, the LEO/USD pair could rally to $6.50 and then to the pattern target at $6.90.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price once again turns down from $6, it will suggest that bears are defending this level with vigor. The sellers will then attempt to sink the price below the 20-day EMA and challenge the 50-day SMA ($5.24).\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDYvYWU0YzQ2OGItNjZmZi00OTk3LThkYTItNzEyMjMzNmEwYWZiLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220629ei6t000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Different this time? 'Almost all' Bitcoin metrics are now hinting at a price bottom\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By William Suberg \par \uc2 641 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 June 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 BTC price could have reached a "logical place" for a reversal as Bitcoin metrics hit the floor.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) played wait-and-see with traders on June 28 as Wall Street opened to flat performance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/23a76df4-e8b7-44b9-8309-494a7da73ace.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 1-hour candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Bollinger eyes "logical place" for Bitcoin bottom\par \par \uc2 Data from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.cointelegraph.com/?via=markets&_ga=2.142027444.742658523.1640948929-762064149.1640948929"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph Markets Pro}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSD/?exchange=BINANCE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\uc2  showed BTC/USD circling $21,000 on \uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 , refusing to commit to a firm trend.\par \par \uc2 The pair nonetheless {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-dips-under-21k-while-exchanges-see-record-outflow-trend"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 avoided}}}\uc2  fresh signs of weakness, leading Cointelegraph contributor Micha\u235\'00\'EBl van de Poppe to believe that an attack on important levels \u8212\'20\'14 notably the 200-week moving average near $22,400 \u8212\'20\'14 could be next.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Bitcoin?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Bitcoin}}}\uc2  bounced upwards after sweeping the lows at $20.6K.\par \par \uc2 Honestly, was expecting a further correction towards $20.3K.\par \par \uc2 Still long on my positions on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24FTM&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $FTM}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ADA&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $\b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24AVAX&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $AVAX}}}\uc2  & {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ETH&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ETH}}}\uc2 , as I'm still assuming we'll see continuation towards $22.4K and possibly $23.1K. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dbwYQiuZZL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dbwYQiuZZL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Micha\u235\'00\'EBl van de Poppe (@CryptoMichNL) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1541773607176740864?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 "In the past, Bitcoin has been a steal under its realized price, i.e., aggregate cost basis of all coins in supply. The realized price is currently sitting at around $22,500," popular trading account Game of Trades {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GameofTrades_/status/1541783486498873345"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GameofTrades_/status/1541783486498873345/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/GameofTrades_/status/1541783486498873345/photo/1}}}\par \par \uc2 While few expected a clear \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend to emerge, long-term perspectives also placed importance on current price levels.\par \par \uc2 Among them was \uc2 John Bollinger\uc2 , creator of the Bollinger bands \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicator, who in a fresh take on BTC/USD flagged the culmination of a trend years in the making.\par \par \uc2 The next move, he suggested, could well be higher after a "picture perfect" double top pattern on Bitcoin in 2021.\par \par \uc2 Picture perfect double (M-type) top in BTCUSD on the monthly chart complete with confirmation by BandWidth and %b leads to a tag of the lower Bollinger Band. No sign of one yet, but this would be a logical place to put in a bottom. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KsDyQsCO1F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/KsDyQsCO1F}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 John Bollinger\uc2  (@bbands) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bbands/status/1541443714886684673?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Research: "Almost all" Bitcoin metrics at all-time lows\par \par \uc2 Further analysis of whether the bottom is in for Bitcoin came from on-chain analytics firm Glassnode as the week began.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/3-charts-showing-this-bitcoin-price-drop-is-unlike-summer-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3 charts showing this Bitcoin \b  \highlight22price drop\b0 \highlight22  is unlike summer 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 In its latest weekly newsletter, "The Week On-Chain," Glassnode {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://insights.glassnode.com/the-week-onchain-week-26-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dissected}}}\uc2  a raft of on-chain metrics in various stages of signaling a bottom formation.\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-climbs-to-22-5k-after-fed-75-basis-point-hike-aims-to-cap-runaway-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unprecedented macro environment}}}\uc2 , however, nothing was certain.\par \par \uc2 "Within the current macroeconomic framework, all models and historical precedents are likely to be put to the test," it concluded.\par \par \uc2 "Based on the current positioning of Bitcoin prices relative to historical floor models, the market is already at an extremely improbable level, with only 0.2% of trading days being in similar circumstances."\par \par \uc2 It noted that those who had bought BTC in 2020 and 2021 had provided the driving force behind recent selling.\par \par \uc2 "Almost all macro indicators for Bitcoin, ranging from technical to on-chain, are at all-time lows, coincident with bear market floor formation in previous cycles. Many are trading at levels with just single-digit percentage points of prior history at similar levels," the newsletter added.\par \par \uc2 Sentiment was no different on the day, with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://alternative.me/crypto/fear-and-greed-index/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto Fear & Greed Index}}}\uc2  at 10/100 or "extreme fear," also constituting a classic reversal level in bear markets gone by.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/5e34f8a2-6b06-42af-ad24-531b81ab6e8c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto Fear & Greed Index (screenshot). Source: Alternative.me\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph.com. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDYvOTg5NTAwM2MtNjIyMC00MmU1LWIxY2UtZTZmMzY5NDUzNGExLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220628ei6s0008d\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 6/27: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, DOGE, DOT, SHIB, AVAX\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,822 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 June 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and altcoins are facing profit-booking after the recent relief rally, but charts suggest that revisit to recent swing lows could be in store.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/2022-bear-market-has-been-the-worst-on-record-glassnode"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 current bear market is one of the worst}}}\uc2 , according to a report by on-chain analytics firm Glassnode. This was the first time in history that the Mayer Multiple slipped below the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-for-beginners/bitcoin-halving-how-does-the-halving-cycle-work-and-why-does-it-matter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previous cycle\u8217\'20\'19s low}}}\uc2 . Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s fall below $20,000 on June 18 also marked the biggest loss ever booked by investors in a single day at $4.23 billion. Considering the above factors and a few other events, Glassnode believes that the capitulation in Bitcoin may have started.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin whales seem to have started their purchasing, suggesting that the bottom may be close and on June 25, analytics resource "Game of Trades" highlighted that demand from whales holding 1,000 to 10,000 Bitcoin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-tops-10-day-highs-as-bitcoin-whale-demand-sees-huge-spike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 witnessed a sharp spike in demand}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/c7c8f554-05be-4fc7-87ba-d79fe264d111.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Another sign that traders are purchasing comes from Glassnode comments suggesting that the 30-day average change in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-dips-under-21k-while-exchanges-see-record-outflow-trend"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supply kept on exchanges plummeted by 153,849 Bitcoin}}}\uc2  on June 26, the largest ever in history.\par \par \uc2 Could bulls continue their purchases on dips and form a higher low? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin turned down from $22,000 on June 26, indicating that the sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on minor rallies. The bears will try to pull the price to the psychological level of $20,000.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/44b8ee6d-9415-40d8-9731-498fe3828dd2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off $20,000, it will suggest that bulls are accumulating on dips. That could keep the pair range-bound between $20,000 and $22,000 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of strength will be a break and close above the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($22,890). That could open the doors for a possible rally to the 50% Fibonacci retracement level at $24,693.\par \par \uc2 This level could again act as a resistance, but if bulls overcome the barrier, the BTC/USDT pair could rally to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA)($27,150). The bulls will have to push the price above this level to indicate that the pair may have bottomed out.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) reached the 20-day EMA ($1,300) on June 26 but the bulls could not push the price above the resistance. This suggests that the bears are not willing to surrender their advantage easily.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/ae4969cc-11bd-4c26-aceb-34d36ff12aec.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the current level, the bears will try to pull the ETH/USDT pair to $1,050. This is an important level to watch out for because a break below it could suggest that bears are in control.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns up from the current level or rises from $1,050, the bulls will try to propel the pair above the 20-day EMA. If they manage to do that, the pair could rally to the breakdown level of $1,700. A break and close above this resistance could indicate the start of a new uptrend.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  has been clinging to the 20-day EMA ($241) since June 24. This suggests that the bears are defending the level but the bulls have not yet given up as they anticipate a move higher.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/4f445ce3-2f49-421f-b402-b4e60857c865.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If buyers thrust the price above the 20-day EMA, the BNB/USDT pair could rally to the 50-day SMA ($277). This level may again act as a stiff hurdle but if crossed, the pair could attempt a rally toward $350.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the current level, the pair could drop to $211. This is an important level to keep an eye on because a rebound off it will suggest that bulls are attempting to form a higher low. But if the level cracks, the pair could retest the vital support at $183.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) broke and closed above the overhead resistance at $0.35 on June 24 but the bulls could not clear the barrier at the 50-day SMA ($0.38). This suggests that the bears are defending the level aggressively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/1f0cd46a-5d5f-4fb9-a8a8-bd0dc3adfb82.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A minor positive is that the bulls have not allowed the price to dip back below the 20-day EMA ($0.35). This suggests buying on dips. If the price rebounds off the current level, the bulls will again attempt to push the price above the 50-day SMA.\par \par \uc2 If they can pull it off, it will suggest that the downtrend could be weakening. The XRP/USDT pair could then rise to $0.45.\par \par \uc2 Another possibility is that bears pull the price back below $0.35. If that happens, the pair could slide to $0.32 and then to $0.28.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 The buyers pushed Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($0.50) on June 26 but the long wick on the candlestick shows that bears aggressively sold at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/7b2348e8-80ef-4bba-b3b0-494535303f5f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A minor positive is that the bulls have not given up ground and are again attempting to clear the overhead hurdle at the moving averages. If they succeed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could rise toward $0.70 where the bears may again put up a strong defense.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down sharply from this level, it will suggest that the pair may remain range-bound between $0.40 and $0.70 for some more time.\par \par \uc2 This positive view could be negated in the short term if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below $0.44. That could pull the pair to $0.40.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) has been stuck between the moving averages since June 24. This suggests that bears are selling on rallies to the 50-day SMA ($43) and bulls are buying on dips to the 20-day EMA ($38).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/af65a4ba-de0b-4c33-85fe-53266f92d76b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are close to a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the relative strength index (RSI) is near the midpoint, suggesting that bulls are attempting a comeback. If buyers propel the price above the 50-day SMA, the SOL/USDT pair could rise to $60.\par \par \uc2 This level may again act as a stiff resistance but if bulls clear this hurdle, the momentum could pick up. On the contrary, if the price turns down and plunges below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that bears have overpowered the bulls. The pair could then slide to $33.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) broke and closed above the 20-day EMA ($0.07) on June 25. The buyers extended the recovery on June 26 and pushed the price to the 50-day SMA ($0.08) but the long wick on the candlestick suggests that bears are defending the level with vigor.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/e89ffa82-7bce-417e-a7be-130ba2ebff65.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The buyers are again trying to push the price above the 50-day SMA. If they manage to do that, the DOT/USDT pair could rally to $0.09 and then to the psychological level at $0.10. This level could again act as a resistance but if bulls overcome this barrier, the momentum is likely to pick up.\par \par \uc2 Alternately, if the price fails to sustain above the 50-day SMA, it will suggest that bears continue to sell on rallies. The bears will then try to pull the price back below the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/dogecoin-price-could-rally-20-in-july-with-this-bullish-reversal-pattern"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin price could rally 20% in July with this \b  \highlight22bullish\b0 \highlight22  reversal pattern}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bears have been aggressively defending the 20-day EMA ($8.11) in Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) since June 24 but a positive sign is that bulls have not given up much ground. A tight consolidation near a resistance usually resolves to the upside.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/84fb7afa-049f-4581-aa2b-a238fbd5f630.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If buyers drive the price above the 20-day EMA, the DOT/USDT pair could rise to the 50-day SMA ($9.13). This level may again act as a hurdle but the likelihood of a break above it is high. If that happens, the pair could rally to $10.75.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that bears are active at higher levels. The sellers will then try to pull the pair below $7.30 and challenge the crucial support at $6.36.\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Shiba Inu ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/shiba-inu-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SHIB}}}\uc2  ) broke above the 50-day SMA ($0.000011) on June 25 but the bulls could not continue the recovery. The bears sold near $0.000012 on June 26 and are trying to pull the price back below the 50-day SMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/7b04c696-b750-48fb-8abf-2164583ce553.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.000010) has started to turn up gradually and the RSI is in the positive territory. This suggests that buyers have a slight edge. If the price rebounds off the current level or the 20-day EMA, the bulls will again attempt to resume the up-move.\par \par \uc2 If the price rises above $0.000012, the SHIB/USDT pair could rally to the overhead resistance at $0.000014. This positive view could be negated in the short term if the price turns down and plummets below the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) has been stuck in a tight range between the 20-day EMA ($20) and the overhead resistance at $21.35 since June 25. This suggests indecision among the bulls and the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/390e0ac7-b55b-41de-a6d9-d0b917edb15c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI is just below the midpoint, which suggests an equilibrium between buyers and sellers. If bulls push the price above $21.35, the AVAX/USDT pair could rally to the 50-day SMA ($25). This level may act as a minor hurdle but if crossed, the pair may rise to $30.\par \par \uc2 This positive view could invalidate in the short term if the price turns down from the current level or the 50-day SMA and plummets below the 20-day EMA. That could open the doors for a possible decline to $16.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDYvZDY0MmNlNzEtYmIxZi00NzhlLTlkZGEtNTQxNzVmMDJjNWE2LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220627ei6r000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 6/24: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, DOGE, DOT, SHIB, LEO\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,812 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A handful of on-chain metrics suggest that Bitcoin could be close to bottoming, and if true, the eventual relief rally could induce sharp gains from altcoins.\par \par \uc2 The United States equity markets and the cryptocurrency space are witnessing a relief rally this week. Supporting the rise in risky assets is the U.S. dollar index (DXY), which retreated from its multi-year high. Generally, cryptocurrencies move inverse to the price of the U.S. dollar, but this week's bounce does not necessarily mean that bulls' grip over the market has come to an end.\par \par \uc2 Citing on-chain data, CryptoQuant senior analyst Julio Moreno, said that Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-miner-capitulation-event-may-have-already-happened-research"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 miners may have already capitulated}}}\uc2 . Historical data {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-for-beginners/how-to-mine-bitcoin-a-beginners-guide-to-mine-btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggests that miner}}}\uc2  capitulation usually precedes market bottoms.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/d2edd3ac-734f-4e16-ae43-ce3f65e20cb1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Another on-chain metric which indicates that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-hodler-data-hints-btc-price-really-close-to-bottom-analysts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s price may have reached an attractive level}}}\uc2  is the Mayer Multiple. The metric is calculated by dividing the price of Bitcoin by the 200-day moving average value. It points to whether Bitcoin is overbought, undervalued or fairly priced. On June 22, the indicator's reading was 0.5 and according to crypto entrepreneur Kyle Chasse, Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s price has dipped below this reading only on 3% of all trading days.\par \par \uc2 Several on-chain indicators are suggesting that Bitcoin may be close to a bottom. Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out what the technicals suggest?\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin is attempting a recovery in a downtrend but the bulls are struggling to push the price to the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $23,024. This suggests that demand dries up at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/8d2e3c3b-b908-4095-97b2-494089d9a3d8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The first hurdle for the bulls is likely to be $21,723 and then the 20-day exponential moving average ($23,529). During strong downtrends, bears sell on rallies to this level. Hence, it becomes an important level to keep an eye on.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down sharply from the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the bears are in command. The sellers will then make another attempt to sink the BTC/USDT pair to the crucial level at $17,622.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if buyers propel the price above the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the bears may be losing their grip. That could open the doors for a possible rally to the 50-day simple moving average ($27,995).\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) had been trading between $1,200 and $1,050 since June 20. This tight range trading resolved to the upside on June 24 as bulls attempt to push the price to the 20-day EMA ($1,332).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/30011f91-11a1-49bd-bafa-515c11a2cdb6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This level is likely to attract strong resistance from the bears. If the price turns down sharply from the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on rallies.\par \par \uc2 The bears will then try to pull the price to $1,050. A break and close below this support could retest the vital support at $881.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if bulls drive the price above the 20-day EMA, the likelihood of a rally to the breakdown level of $1,700 increases.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bears tried to pull Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) below $211 on June 22 but the bulls held their ground. This started a relief rally which has reached the 20-day EMA ($243).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/76bbd6f5-62c7-4a96-9e06-df915b3958f5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bulls push the price above the 20-day EMA, it will increase the possibility that the break below $211 may have been a bear trap. The BNB/USDT pair could then rally to the 50-day SMA ($284) where the bears may again mount a strong resistance.\par \par \uc2 Another possibility is that the price turns down sharply from the 20-day EMA. If that happens, the bears will try to pull the pair below $211 and challenge the June 18 intraday low of $183. A break below this support could indicate the start of a downtrend to $150.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 The tight range trading in Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) resolved to the upside with a break above the 20-day EMA ($0.35) on June 24. This suggests that the bears may be losing their grip.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/cc357548-9e84-4ebb-b5ce-4af1342b891d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The buyers tried to propel the price above the 50-day SMA ($0.40) on June 24 but the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick suggests that bears continue to defend the level aggressively. If the price turns down and breaks below the 20-day EMA, the XRP/USDT pair could drop to $0.35.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns up and breaks above the 50-day SMA, it will suggest the start of a new up-move. The pair could first rally to $0.46 and then make a dash toward $0.56.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has been oscillating between the 20-day EMA ($0.50) and the strong support of $0.44 for the past few days but this tight range trading is unlikely to continue for long.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/fb86822b-47c2-4040-83b0-c85a1bd11327.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The RSI has been gradually climbing higher suggesting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could be weakening. That enhances the prospects of a break above the moving averages. If that happens, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could climb toward $0.70.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that bears are defending the level aggressively. The sellers will then try to pull the pair below the strong support zone of $0.44 to $0.40 and resume the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 20-day EMA ($36) on June 22 but the bears could not sustain the lower levels. The bulls purchased the dip and pushed the price back above the 20-day EMA on June 23.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/686348e7-6c7c-4865-b44e-67f1f55220f8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bulls sustain the price above the 20-day EMA, the SOL/USDT pair could rise to the 50-day SMA ($45). The flattish 20-day EMA and the RSI near the midpoint suggest that the bears may be losing their grip. A break and close above the 50-day SMA will indicate that the downtrend could be over.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price fails to sustain above the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that bears are active at higher levels. If sellers pull the price below $33, the pair could slide to $27.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) has been trading near the 20-day EMA ($0.06) since June 21. This suggests that the bulls are not closing their positions as they anticipate a break above the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/2cb3373b-1b14-46b9-9c9e-598275562a9a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The RSI has been gradually rising toward the midpoint and the 20-day EMA is flattening out, which suggests that the bulls are attempting a comeback.\par \par \uc2 If bulls thrust the price above the 20-day EMA, the DOGE/USDT pair could rally to the 50-day SMA ($0.08) where the bears may again pose a strong challenge. The bulls will have to clear this hurdle to open the doors for a possible up-move to $0.10.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, the bears will try to pull the pair below $0.06 and challenge the psychological support at $0.05.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-gives-encouraging-signs-watch-these-btc-price-levels-next"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin gives \u8216\'20\'18encouraging signs\u8217\'20\'19 \u8212\'20\'14 Watch these BTC price levels next}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the $7.30 support on June 23 indicating that bulls are attempting to form a higher low. The price has reached the 20-day EMA ($8.15), which is an important barrier for the bulls to overcome.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/8965a002-853b-454a-a10f-a7670b0138f3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The RSI has risen above 45 and the 20-day EMA is flattening out. This suggests that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could be weakening. If bulls push the price above the moving averages, the DOT/USDT pair could attempt a rally to the overhead resistance at $12.44.\par \par \uc2 This level may again act as a strong resistance and if the price turns down from it, the pair could remain stuck between $12.44 and $7.30 for a few days. The bears will have to sink the price below the $7.30 to $6.36 support zone to indicate the start of the next leg of the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bears tried to pull the price below the 20-day EMA ($0.000009) on June 22 but the bulls held their ground. Shiba Inu ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/shiba-inu-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SHIB}}}\uc2  ) rebounded off the 20-day EMA on June 23 but the buyers could not push the price above the 50-day SMA ($0.000011).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/b8462550-e6cc-4236-8495-35510e16718e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI is just above the midpoint, indicating equilibrium between buyers and sellers. This balance could tilt in favor of the bulls if they propel the price above the 50-day SMA. The SHIB/USDT pair could then rally to the overhead resistance at $0.000014.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down and plummets below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that bears have gained the upper hand. The pair could then slide to $0.000008.\par \par \uc2 LEO/USD\par \par \uc2 UNUS SED LEO ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/leo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LEO}}}\uc2  ) repeatedly rose above the resistance line of the descending channel between June 22 and June 24 but the bulls could not sustain the higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/3a5eab05-5814-48a6-8157-7a9bfb060c45.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LEO/USD daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This suggests that the bears are aggressively defending the resistance line of the channel. The failure to sustain the price above the channel may tempt short-term traders to book profits.\par \par \uc2 That could pull the price to the 20-day EMA ($5.39). If the price rebounds off this support, the bulls will again attempt to push the LEO/USD pair above the channel. If they succeed, the next stop could be $6.50 and then $6.80.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns down and breaks below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the pair may remain stuck inside the channel for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDYvZDM1ZjUxNjMtZDNhMi00ZmMxLTk3NDQtMmJjNTYwZmQ2NTAxLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220624ei6o000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 On the brink of recession: Can Bitcoin survive its first global economic crisis?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Yashu Gola \par \uc2 1,364 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 June 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has not seen a single full-blown recession in its lifetime but analysts see it surviving one after suffering more blows.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) was a response to the 2008 global recession. It introduced a new way to transact without depending on the trust of third parties, such as banks, particularly failing banks that were nevertheless bailed out by the government at the expense of the public.\par \par \uc2 "The central bank must be trusted not to debase the currency, but the history of fiat currencies is full of breaches of that trust," \uc2 Satoshi Nakamoto{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://p2pfoundation.ning.com/forum/topics/bitcoin-open-source"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in 2009.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin's genesis block sums up the intent with the following embedded message:\par \par \uc2 "The Times 03/Jan/2009 Chancellor on brink of second bailout for banks."\par \par \uc2 But while Bitcoin keeps mining blocks unfazed, and its gold-like properties have attracted investors seeking "digital gold," its current 75% comedown from $69,000 highs in November 2021 demonstrates that its not immune to global economic forces.\par \par \uc2 Simultaneously, the entire crypto market lost $2.25 trillion in the same period, hinting at large-scale demand destruction in the industry.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin's crash appeared during the period of rising inflation and the global central banks' hawkish response to it. Notably, the \uc2 Federal Reserve{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-climbs-to-22-5k-after-fed-75-basis-point-hike-aims-to-cap-runaway-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hiked its benchmark rates by 75 basis points}}}\uc2  (bps) on June 15 to curb inflation that reached 8.4% in May.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/2f3809f3-011b-42ba-964d-5ef8d6fdd8ba.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily price chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, the crash left BTC trending even more in-sync with the tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite's performance. The U.S. stock market index fell over 30% between November 2021 and June 2022.\par \par \uc2 More rate hikes ahead\par \par \uc2 Fed Chairman \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  noted in his Congressional testimony that their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-rises-to-20-7k-as-fed-s-powell-says-more-rate-hikes-appropriate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rate hikes would continue to bring down inflation}}}\uc2 , albeit adding that "the pace of those changes will continue to depend on the incoming data and the evolving outlook for the economy."\par \par \uc2 The statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/markets/europe/fed-lift-rates-by-75-basis-points-july-50-bps-september-2022-06-22/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 followed}}}\uc2  Reuters' poll of economists, which agreed that the Fed would raise benchmark rates by another 75 bps in July and will follow it up with a 0.5% increase in September.\par \par \uc2 That adds more downside potential to an already-declining crypto market, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-06-22/bitcoin-sinks-again-as-risk-off-mood-returns-on-recession-fears?srnd=cryptocurrencies-v2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  Informa Global Markets, a London-based financial intelligence firm, saying that it would not bottom out until the Fed subsides its "aggressive approach to monetary policy."\par \par \uc2 But a U-turn on hawkish policies seems unlikely in the near term, given the central bank's 2% inflation target. Interestingly, the gap between the Fed's fund rates and the consumer price index (CPI) is now the largest on record.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/8be5b6f3-fe28-4d72-aee3-0dc6dde70ffb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Fed funds rate versus inflation. Source: Ecoinometrics\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin faces first potential recession\par \par \uc2 Nearly 70% of economists believe that the U.S. economy will slip into a recession next year due to a hawkish Fed, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/53fcbbf1-39e3-483c-a6f2-b0de432ed5a3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to a survey of 49 respondents conducted by the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 To recap, a country enters a recession when its economy faces a negative gross domestic product (GDP), coupled with rising unemployment levels, declining retail sales and a lower manufacturing output for an extended period of time.\par \par \uc2 Notably, about 38% expect the recession to begin in the first half of 2023, while 30% anticipate the same to happen during the Q3\u8211\'20\'13Q4 session. Moreover, a separate survey {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-05-13/odds-of-a-us-recession-within-next-year-now-30-survey-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conducted}}}\uc2  by \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  in May shows a 30% possibility of recession next year.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/c8865638-6e4c-470e-a6ac-f08be8ecc54d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 The next recession in the U.S. will begin in 2023. Source: \uc2 Financial Times\par \par \uc2 Powell also noted in his June 22 press conference that recession is "certainly a possibility" due to "events of the last few months around the world," i.e., the Ukraine-Russia war, wh has caused a food and oil crisis around the globe.\par \par \uc2 The predictions risk putting Bitcoin before a full-blown economic crisis. And the fact it has not behaved anything {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-not-a-safe-haven-but-maybe-something-more"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 like a safe-haven asset}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-not-a-safe-haven-but-maybe-something-more"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-not-a-safe-haven-but-maybe-something-more}}}\uc2  during the period of rising inflation increases the probability that it will keep declining alongside the Wall Street indexes, primarily tech stocks.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/investors-dumping-on-terra-as-luna-2-tanks-70-in-two-days"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collapse of Terra}}}\uc2  (LUNA, since renamed LUNC), a $40-billion "algorithmic stablecoin" project, which led to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/finance-redefined-three-arrow-capital-and-celsius-fall-brings-a-tsunami-of-sell-off-in-defi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 insolvency issues in Three Arrow Capital}}}\uc2 , the largest crypto hedge fund, has also destroyed demand across the crypto sector.\par \par \uc2 For instance, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), the second-largest cryptocurrency after Bitcoin, dropped by more than 80% to $880 lows during the ongoing bear cycle.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, other top-ranking digital assets, including Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) and Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ), plunged in the range of 85% to over 90% from their 2021 peaks.\par \par \uc2 "The crypto house is on fire, and everyone is just, you know, rushing to the exits because there's just completely lost confidence in the space," {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/06/14/1105025475/a-crypto-winter-or-a-meltdown-recession-fears-and-layoffs-hit-crypto-currencies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 Edward Moya\uc2 , a senior markets analyst at \uc2 OANDA\uc2 , an online forex brokerage.\par \par \uc2 BTC bear markets are nothing new\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-may-bottom-at-15-5k-if-it-retests-this-lifetime-historical-support-level"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Incoming \b  \highlight22bearish\b0 \highlight22  predictions}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-may-bottom-at-15-5k-if-it-retests-this-lifetime-historical-support-level"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-may-bottom-at-15-5k-if-it-retests-this-lifetime-historical-support-level}}}\uc2  for Bitcoin envision the price to break below its $20,000-support level, with Leigh Drogen, general partner and CIO at Starkiller Capital, a digital assets quantitative hedge fund, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fortune.com/2022/06/17/crypto-quant-fund-manager-bitcoin-price-prediction/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anticipating}}}\uc2  that the coin will reach $10,000, down 85% from its peak level.\par \par \uc2 However, there is little evidence for Bitcoin's total demise, especially after the coin's confrontation with six bear markets (based on its 20%-plus corrections) in the past, each leading to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-correction-continues-dashing-hopes-of-20k-in-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rally above the previous record high}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/647fc11d-419a-4bf8-8a70-9c788a7af68f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BravenewCoin Liquid Index featuring Bitcoin's bear market since 2011. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Nick, an analyst at data resource Ecoinometrics, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ecoinometrics.substack.com/p/ecoinometrics-bear-market-mindset"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sees}}}\uc2  Bitcoin behaving like a stock market index, still in the "middle of an adoption curve."\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin is likely to drop further in a higher interest rate environment \u8212\'20\'14 similar to how the U.S. benchmark S&P 500 has dipped multiple times in the last 100 years \u8212\'20\'14 only to recover strongly.\par \par \uc2 Excerpts:\par \par \uc2 "Between 1929 and 2022, the S&P500 is up 200x. That\u8217\'20\'19s something like a 6% annualized rate of return [...]. Some of those asymmetric bets are obvious and pretty safe, like buying Bitcoin now."\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/a1647809-cc81-44a1-a584-24727379be9a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 S&P 500 drawdowns throughout its history. Source: Ecoinometrics\par \par \uc2 Most altcoins will die\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, the same cannot be said about all the coins in the crypto market. Many of these so-called alternative cryptocurrencies, or "altcoins," have dropped to their deaths this year, ith some low-cap coins, in particular, logging over 99% price declines.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/f34bfd84-a1d7-48af-bb18-5e8a7c69d33a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Altcoins that heave faced nearly 100% losses in 2022. Source: Messari\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, projects with healthy adoption rates and real users could come out on top in the wake of a potential global economic crisis.\par \par \uc2 The top candidate to date is Ethereum, the leading smart contract platform, which dominates the layer-one blockchain ecosystem with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://defillama.com/chain/Ethereum"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over $46 billion locked}}}\uc2  across its DeFi applications.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/c4e47daf-ae34-4db3-91ed-91722c713538.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Ethereum leads the smart contract sector. Source: DeFi Llama\par \par \uc2 Other chains, including Binance Smart Chain (BSC), Solana, Cardano and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/chainlink-brings-keepers-and-vrf-to-the-avalanche-blockchain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/chainlink-brings-keepers-and-vrf-to-the-avalanche-blockchain}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/chainlink-brings-keepers-and-vrf-to-the-avalanche-blockchain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Avalanche, could also attract}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/solana-nft-marketplace-magic-eden-closes-130m-series-b-round-at-1-6b-valuation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 users as alternatives}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/solana-nft-marketplace-magic-eden-closes-130m-series-b-round-at-1-6b-valuation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ensuring demand for their underlying tokens}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, older altcoins such as Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) also have higher survival chances, particularly with t speculation about possible {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/elon-musk-s-twitter-investment-puts-a-150-rally-into-play-for-dogecoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter integration in the pipeline.}}}\par \par \uc2 Overall, a macro-led bear market will most likely hurt all digital assets across the board in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 But coins with lower market caps, dismissive liquidity and higher \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be at a higher risk of collapse, Alexander Tkachenko, founder and CEO at VNX, a digital gold dealer, told Cointelegraph. He added:\par \par \uc2 "If Bitcoin and other cryptocurrencies want to get back to their full power, they need to become self-sufficient alternatives to fiat currencies, especially the U.S. dollar."\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph.com. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDYvZTQ1MjQ2YTktYjA1Yy00OTRjLWEwY2MtMGUzNzAzNzViOThiLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220623ei6n0008m\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 On the brink of recession: Can Bitcoin survive its first global economic crisis?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Yashu Gola \par \uc2 1,309 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 June 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has not seen a single full-blown recession in its lifetime but analysts see it surviving one after suffering more blows.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) was a response to the 2008 global recession. It introduced a new way to transact without depending on trust of third-parties, such as banks, particularly failing banks that were nevertheless bailed out by government at the expense of the public.\par \par \uc2 "The central bank must be trusted not to debase the currency, but the history of fiat currencies is full of breaches of that trust," \uc2 Satoshi Nakamoto{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://p2pfoundation.ning.com/forum/topics/bitcoin-open-source"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in 2009.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin's genesis block sums up the intent with the following embedded message:\par \par \uc2 The Times 03/Jan/2009 Chancellor on brink of second bailout for banks.\par \par \uc2 But while Bitcoin keeps mining blocks unfazed, and its gold-like properties have attracted investors seeking "digital gold," its current 75% comedown from $69,000 highs in November 2021 demonstrates that its not immune to global economic forces.\par \par \uc2 Simultaneously, the entire crypto market lost $2.25 trillion in the same period, hinting at large-scale demand destruction in the industry.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin's crash appeared during the period of rising inflation and the global central banks' hawkish response to it. Notably, the \uc2 Federal Reserve{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-climbs-to-22-5k-after-fed-75-basis-point-hike-aims-to-cap-runaway-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hiked its benchmark rates by 75 basis points}}}\uc2  (bps) on June 15 to curb inflation that reached 8.4% in May.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/2f3809f3-011b-42ba-964d-5ef8d6fdd8ba.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily price chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, the crash left BTC trending even more in-sync with the tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite's performance. The U.S. stock market index fell over 30% between November 2021 and June 2022.\par \par \uc2 More rate hikes ahead\par \par \uc2 Fed Chairman \uc2 Jerome Powell{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-rises-to-20-7k-as-fed-s-powell-says-more-rate-hikes-appropriate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  in his Congressional testimony that their rate hikes would continue to bring down inflation, albeit adding that "the pace of those changes will continue to depend on the incoming data and the evolving outlook for the economy."\par \par \uc2 The statement followed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/markets/europe/fed-lift-rates-by-75-basis-points-july-50-bps-september-2022-06-22/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters' poll of economists}}}\uc2  that agreed that the Fed would raise benchmark rates by another 75 bps in July and will follow it up with a 0.5% increase in September.\par \par \uc2 That adds more downside potential to an already-declining crypto market, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-06-22/bitcoin-sinks-again-as-risk-off-mood-returns-on-recession-fears?srnd=cryptocurrencies-v2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  Informa Global Markets, a London-based financial intelligence firm, saying that it would not bottom out until the Fed subsides its "aggressive approach to monetary policy."\par \par \uc2 But a U-turn on hawkish policies seems unlikely in the near term given the central bank's 2% inflation target. Interestingly, the gap between the Fed's fund rates and the consumer price index (CPI) is now the largest on record.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/8be5b6f3-fe28-4d72-aee3-0dc6dde70ffb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Fed funds rate versus inflation. Source: Ecoinometrics\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin faces first potential recession\par \par \uc2 Nearly 70% of economists believe that the U.S. economy will slip into a recession next year due to a hawkish Fed, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/53fcbbf1-39e3-483c-a6f2-b0de432ed5a3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2  of 49 respondents conducted by the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 To recap, a country enters a recession when its economy faces negative gross domestic product (GDP), coupled with rising unemployment levels, declining retail sales, and lower manufacturing output for an extended period of time.\par \par \uc2 Notably, about 38% expect the recession to begin in the first half of 2023, while 30% anticipate the same to happen during the Q3-Q4 session. Moreover, a separate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-05-13/odds-of-a-us-recession-within-next-year-now-30-survey-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2  conducted by \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  in May shows a 30% possibility of recession next year.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/c8865638-6e4c-470e-a6ac-f08be8ecc54d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 The next recession in the U.S. will begin in 2023. Source: \uc2 Financial Times\par \par \uc2 Powell also noted in his June 22 press conference that recession is "certainly a possibility" due to "events of the last few months around the world," i.e., the Ukraine-Russia war that has caused a food and oil crisis around the globe.\par \par \uc2 The predictions risk putting Bitcoin before a full-blown economic crisis. And the fact it has not behaved anything like a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-not-a-safe-haven-but-maybe-something-more"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 safe-haven asset}}}\uc2  during the period of rising inflation increases the probability that it would keep declining alongside the Wall Street indexes, primarily tech stocks.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/investors-dumping-on-terra-as-luna-2-tanks-70-in-two-days"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collapse of Terra}}}\uc2 , a $40-billion "algorithmic stablecoin" project, and it leading to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/finance-redefined-three-arrow-capital-and-celsius-fall-brings-a-tsunami-of-sell-off-in-defi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 insolvency issues in Three Arrow Capital}}}\uc2 , the largest crypto hedge fund, has also destroyed demand across the crypto sector.\par \par \uc2 For instance, Ether, the second-largest cryptocurrency after Bitcoin, dropped by more than 80% to $880 lows during the ongoing bear cycle.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, other top-ranking digital assets, including Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), and Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ), plunged in the range of 85% to over 90% from their 2021 peaks.\par \par \uc2 "The crypto house is on fire, and everyone is just, you know, rushing to the exits because there's just completely lost confidence in the space," {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/06/14/1105025475/a-crypto-winter-or-a-meltdown-recession-fears-and-layoffs-hit-crypto-currencies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 Edward Moya\uc2 , a senior markets analyst at \uc2 OANDA\uc2 , an online forex brokerage.\par \par \uc2 BTC bear markets are nothing new\par \par \uc2 Incoming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-may-bottom-at-15-5k-if-it-retests-this-lifetime-historical-support-level"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22bearish\b0 \highlight22  predictions}}}\uc2  for Bitcoin envision the price to break below its $20,000-support level, with Leigh Drogen, general partner and CIO at Starkiller Capital, a digital assets quantitative hedge fund, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fortune.com/2022/06/17/crypto-quant-fund-manager-bitcoin-price-prediction/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anticipating}}}\uc2  that the coin will reach $10,000, down 85% from its peak level.\par \par \uc2 However, there is little evidence for Bitcoin's total demise, especially after the coin's confrontation with six bear markets (based on its 20%-plus corrections) in the past, each leading to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-correction-continues-dashing-hopes-of-20k-in-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rally above the previous record high}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/647fc11d-419a-4bf8-8a70-9c788a7af68f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BravenewCoin Liquid Index featuring Bitcoin's bear market since 2011. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Nick, an analyst at data resource Ecoinometrics, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ecoinometrics.substack.com/p/ecoinometrics-bear-market-mindset"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sees}}}\uc2  Bitcoin behaving like a stock market index, still in the "middle of an adoption curve."\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin is likely to drop further in a higher interest rate environment\u8212\'20\'14similar to how the U.S. benchmark S&P 500 has dipped multiple times in the last 100 years, only to recover strongly.\par \par \uc2 Excerpts:\par \par \uc2 "Between 1929 and 2022 the S&P500 is up 200x. That\u8217\'20\'19s something like a 6% annualized rate of return [...] Some of those asymmetric bets are obvious and pretty safe, like buying Bitcoin now."\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/a1647809-cc81-44a1-a584-24727379be9a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 S&P 500 drawdowns throughout its history. Source: Ecoinometrics\par \par \uc2 Most altcoins will die\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, the same cannot be said about all the coins in the crypto market. Many of these so-called alternative cryptocurrencies, or "altcoins," have dropped to their deaths this year. With some low-cap coins, in particular, logging over 99% price declines.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/f34bfd84-a1d7-48af-bb18-5e8a7c69d33a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Altcoins that heave faced nearly 100% losses in 2022. Source: Messari\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, projects with healthy adoption rates and real users could come out on top in the wake of a potential global economic crisis.\par \par \uc2 The top candidate to date is Ethereum, the leading smart contract platform, which dominates the layer-one blockchain ecosystem with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://defillama.com/chain/Ethereum"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over $46 billion locked}}}\uc2  across its DeFi applications.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-06/c4e47daf-ae34-4db3-91ed-91722c713538.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Ethereum leads the smart contract sector. Source: DeFi Llama\par \par \uc2 Other chains, including Binance Smart Chain (BSC), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/solana-nft-marketplace-magic-eden-closes-130m-series-b-round-at-1-6b-valuation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/disappointing-cardano-devs-delay-vasil-hard-fork-by-a-month"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointel